msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Safinatun Najah"
msgid ""
"A hardcover English translation of the Safinatun Najah, a renowned manual of "
"Islamic jurisprudence, specifically focusing on the Shafi'i school of "
"thought.  It serves as a comprehensive guide for Muslims seeking knowledge "
"and understanding of the principles and practices of Islam."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Heidelberg Catechism"
msgid_plural "copies of the Heidelberg Catechism"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Heidelberg Catechism"
msgid ""
"A hardcover, updated edition of the 'Heidelberg Catechism', a Protestant "
"confession of faith and also a guide for religious instruction, written in "
"1563 (and also one of the Three Forms of Unity, or Four Forms of Unity, "
"depending on the denomination).  The contents consists of 129 questions and "
"answers, divided into three main sections: guilt, grace, and gratitude.  Each "
"section addresses a different aspect of the Christian faith and is intended "
"to be memorized and understood by believers."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Philaret Catechism"
msgid_plural "copies of the Philaret Catechism"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Philaret Catechism"
msgid ""
"A hardcover English translation of the Philaret Catechism, written by the "
"Metropolitan Philaret of Moscow in the 19th century.  This book serves as a "
"comprehensive guide to the teachings and beliefs of the Eastern Orthodox "
"Church, structured in a question-and-answer format and covers various aspects "
"of Christian doctrine, including theology, morality, sacraments, prayer, and "
"the Ten Commandments."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Keach's Catechism"
msgid_plural "copies of the Keach's Catechism"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Keach's Catechism"
msgid ""
"A hardcover edition of the Keach's Catechism, a Reformed Baptist catechism "
"consisting of a set of basic questions and answers from scripture teaching "
"readers the basics of the Baptist faith."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Pentecostal Catechism"
msgid_plural "copies of the Pentecostal Catechism"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Pentecostal Catechism"
msgid ""
"A hardcover edition of the Pentecostal Catechism, a comprehensive guide to "
"the beliefs, practices, and teachings of the Pentecostal movement within "
"Christianity."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Canons of Dort"
msgid_plural "copies of the Canons of Dort"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Canons of Dort"
msgid ""
"A rare English translation of the Canons of Dort, a significant theological "
"document within the Reformed tradition.  It consists of five main points: The "
"Corruption of Human Nature, Unconditional Election, Limited Atonement, "
"Irresistible Grace and Perseverance of the Saints.  It is also one of the "
"Three Forms of Unity, or Four Forms of Unity, depending on the denomination."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Confession of Faith"
msgid_plural "copies of the Confession of Faith"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Confession of Faith"
msgid ""
"A rare English translation of the Confession of Faith, also known as the "
"Belgic Confession.  It is a collection of documents in Christian theology and "
"written statements of belief or doctrines.  These confessions aim to "
"summarize and articulate the core beliefs of particular Christian "
"denominations and traditions.  It also serve as a guide for the members of "
"the church to understand and uphold the essential teachings of their faith.  "
"It is also one of the Three Forms of Unity, or Four Forms of Unity, depending "
"on the denomination."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "The Orthodox Church"
msgid_plural "copies of The Orthodox Church"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "The Orthodox Church"
msgid ""
"A paperback edition of 'The Orthodox Church: An Introduction to Eastern "
"Christianity', written by Timothy Ware.  This book provides a comprehensive "
"overview of the history, theology, and practices of the Eastern Orthodox "
"Church, and an introduction to the Orthodox faith for those unfamiliar with "
"it, as well as a deeper exploration for those seeking to deepen their "
"understanding."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Didascalia Apostolorum"
msgid_plural "copies of the Didascalia Apostolorum"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Didascalia Apostolorum"
msgid ""
"A paperback English translation of the Didascalia Apostolorum, an ancient "
"Christian text that provides instructions and guidelines for the organization "
"and governance of the early Christian Church.  The Didascalia Apostolorum is "
"attributed to the Twelve Apostles, and is believed to have been written in "
"the third century AD."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "The Ladder of Divine Ascent"
msgid_plural "copies of The Ladder of Divine Ascent"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "The Ladder of Divine Ascent"
msgid ""
"A commercial-grade, hardcover English edition of The Ladder of Divine Ascent, "
"a well-known spiritual guidebook written in the 6th century by John Climacus, "
"an Orthodox Christian monk.  This book is composed of many chapters, each "
"representing a rung on the ladder, symbolizing the spiritual journey towards "
"union with God."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Jaiva Dharma"
msgid_plural "copies of the Jaiva Dharma"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Jaiva Dharma"
msgid ""
"A paperback English translation of the Jaiva Dharma, a significant "
"philosophical and devotional book written by Srila Bhaktivinoda Thakura, a "
"prominent spiritual leader and philosopher in the Gaudiya Vaishnava Hindu "
"tradition.  This book delves into the essential teachings of the "
"Bhagavad-gita and the Srimad-Bhagavatam, providing deep insights into the "
"nature of the soul, its relationship with God, and the process of spiritual "
"realization."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Book of the Counsels of Zoroaster"
msgid_plural "copies of the Book of the Counsels of Zoroaster"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Book of the Counsels of Zoroaster"
msgid ""
"This is a rare English translation of the 'Book of the Counsels of "
"Zoroaster', also known as 'Pand-namag i Zardust', a post-Sasanian compendium "
"of apothegms intended to instruct every Zoroastrian male, upon his attaining "
"the age of fifteen years, in fundamental religious and ethical principles, as "
"well as in the daily duties incumbent upon him."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Anglican Book of Common Prayer"
msgid_plural "copies of the Anglican Book of Common Prayer"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Anglican Book of Common Prayer"
msgid ""
"A hardcover edition of the Anglican Book of Common Prayer.  It once held "
"great significance in the Anglican Church, but still contain a collection of "
"liturgical prayers, rites, catechisms and instructions that provide a "
"standardized format for various religious services and ceremonies."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Kebra Negast"
msgid_plural "copies of the Kebra Negast"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Kebra Negast"
msgid ""
"A hardcover English translation of the Kebra Negast, also known as the Glory "
"of the Kings.  It is an ancient Ethiopian text that holds significant "
"religious and historical value for the Ethiopian Orthodox Church and the "
"Rastafarian movement.  It is a compilation of sacred stories and legends that "
"revolve around the life of King Solomon and the Queen of Sheba, as well as "
"the birth and early life of King Menelik I, the founder of the Ethiopian "
"Empire."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "The Guru Granth Sahib"
msgid_plural "copies of The Guru Granth Sahib"
msgstr[0] "Sri Guru Granth Sahib"
msgstr[1] "księgi Sri Guru Granth Sahib"
msgstr[2] "ksiąg Sri Guru Granth Sahib"
msgstr[3] "księgi Sri Guru Granth Sahib"

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "The Guru Granth Sahib"
msgid "A single-volume copy of the central religious texts of Sikhism."
msgstr "Pojedyncza księga z kopią centralnego tekstu religijnego sikhizmu."

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Hadith"
msgid_plural "copies of Hadith"
msgstr[0] "Hadis"
msgstr[1] "Hadisy"
msgstr[2] "Hadisów"
msgstr[3] "Hadisu"

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Hadith"
msgid ""
"A Muslim religious text containing an account of the sayings and actions of "
"the prophet Muhammad."
msgstr "Muzułmański tekst religijny o przypowieściach i działaniach proroka Mahometa."

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Principia Discordia"
msgid_plural "copies of Principia Discordia"
msgstr[0] "Principia Discordia"
msgstr[1] "księgi Principia Discordia"
msgstr[2] "ksiąg Principia Discordia"
msgstr[3] "księgi Principia Discordia"

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Principia Discordia"
msgid ""
"A book that embodies the main beliefs of Discordianism.  It seems to "
"primarily concern chaos, and features a card in the back which informs you "
"that you are now a 'genuine and authorized Pope of Discordia'."
msgstr ""
"Księga oddająca główne założenia wiary dyskordianizmu. Wygląda to na teorię "
"chaosu i zawiera kartę na końcu, która informuje wszem i wobec, że jesteś "
"teraz niepodważalnym i zatwierdzonym papieżem Dyskordii."

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "The Kojiki"
msgid_plural "copies of The Kojiki"
msgstr[0] "Kojiki"
msgstr[1] "księgi Kojiki"
msgstr[2] "ksiąg Kojiki"
msgstr[3] "księgi Kojiki"

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "The Kojiki"
msgid ""
"The oldest extant chronicle of Japan's myths and history, the stories "
"contained in the Kojiki are part of the inspiration behind Shinto practices."
msgstr ""
"Najstarsza historyczna kronika japońskich mitów i historii. Zawarte w niej "
"opowieści są częściowo inspiracją stojącą za praktykami szintoizmu."

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Nihon Shoki"
msgid_plural "copies of the Nihon Shoki"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Nihon Shoki"
msgid ""
"Also known as 'Chronicles of Japan', it is considered one of the two most "
"important and oldest chronicles of ancient Japan, the other being the Kojiki. "
" The Nihon Shoki covers the history of Japan with a compilation of myths, "
"legends, religious practices, rituals and historical events."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Fudoki"
msgid_plural "copies of the Fudoki"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Fudoki"
msgid ""
"A somewhat large paperback book containing a extensive compilation of "
"historical records and chronicles that originated in ancient Japan (probably "
"during the Nara and Heian periods).  It covers local legends, folklore, "
"religious beliefs, agricultural practices, dialects, historical events, "
"quantity and quality of resources, boundaries, topography, climate, flora, "
"fauna, and cultural practices of several Japanese provinces at that time."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Ofudekasi"
msgid_plural "copies of the Ofudekasi"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Ofudekasi"
msgid ""
"A large English translation of the most significant of the three scriptures "
"within the Tenrikyo religious tradition (the other two being the Mikagura-uta "
"and Osashizu).  It serves as an essential text that provides a comprehensive "
"understanding of the fundamental beliefs and doctrines of Tenrikyo."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Mikagura-uta"
msgid_plural "copies of the Mikagura-uta"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Mikagura-uta"
msgid ""
"A English translation of the Mikagura-uta, one of the most significant books "
"within the Tenrikyo Religious Tradition.  It is a collection of hymns and "
"prayers that serve as a guide for the followers of the Tenrikyo."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Osashizu"
msgid_plural "copies of the Osashizu"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Osashizu"
msgid ""
"A English translation of the Osashizu, one of the most significant books "
"within the Tenrikyo Religious Tradition.  It serves as a guide for followers "
"of the religion or people wishing to learn about it, providing spiritual "
"teachings, ethical principles, and practical advice on various aspects of "
"life."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Doctrines of Tenrikyo"
msgid_plural "copies of the Doctrines of Tenrikyo"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Doctrines of Tenrikyo"
msgid ""
"A paperback English translation of Tenrikyo's official doctrine.  This book "
"explains the basic teachings of the Tenrikyo Religious Tradition."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "The Life of Oyasama, Foundress of Tenrikyo"
msgid_plural "copies of The Life of Oyasama, Foundress of Tenrikyo"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "The Life of Oyasama, Foundress of Tenrikyo"
msgid ""
"A paperback English translation of Tenrikyo's hagiography of Miki Nakayama, "
"foundress of the Tenrikyo Religious Tradition."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "The Anecdotes of Oyasama, Foundress of Tenrikyo"
msgid_plural "copies of The Anecdotes of Oyasama, Foundress of Tenrikyo"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "The Anecdotes of Oyasama, Foundress of Tenrikyo"
msgid ""
"A paperback English translation of an anthology of anecdotes about Oyasama "
"that were passed down orally by her first followers and later written down "
"and verified."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Buluotuo"
msgid_plural "copies of the Buluotuo"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Buluotuo"
msgid ""
"This is very rare English translation of the Buluotuo, a sacred epic in "
"Moism, the religion of most Zhuang people, the largest ethnic minority of "
"China.  This book addresses the creation of the Universe and life as well as "
"how to live a religiously meritorious life inside Moism.  This book also "
"contains information on entities, deities, gods, goddesses, prayers, "
"practices and rituals of Moism."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Guodian Texts"
msgid_plural "copies of the Guodian Texts"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Guodian Texts"
msgid ""
"A rare and extensive study and translation of all the manuscripts of The "
"Guodian Chu Slips by Scott Cook.  The original slip-texts include both Taoist "
"and Confucian works that offered fresh information for scholars studying the "
"history of philosophical thought in ancient China."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Popol Vuh"
msgid_plural "copies of the Popol Vuh"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Popol Vuh"
msgid ""
"A English edition of the Popol Vuh, a sacred book of the K'iche' Maya people, "
"a native group from the Guatemalan highlands.  It is a combination of "
"creation myths, historical narratives, and heroic legends that revolve around "
"the K'iche' people's origins, culture, and the deities that govern their "
"universe."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Codex Borbonicus"
msgid_plural "copies of the Codex Borbonicus"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Codex Borbonicus"
msgid ""
"A extremely rare English edition of the Codex Borbonicus, an ancient "
"pre-Columbian Mesoamerican manuscript that provides valuable insights into "
"the religious and ritual practices of the Aztecs.  It contains original "
"pictures, illustrations, detailed information about the tonalpohualli (the "
"sacred 260-day calendar), the xiuhpohualli (the agricultural year), deities, "
"rituals, and ceremonies.  This codex also includes depictions and information "
"of various gods and goddesses, sacrificial rites, and astronomical phenomena."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Huarochirí Manuscript"
msgid_plural "copies of the Huarochirí Manuscript"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Huarochirí Manuscript"
msgid ""
"A uncommon English edition of the Huarochirí Manuscript, a collection of "
"Quechua narratives that provides valuable insights into the religious "
"beliefs, rituals, and cosmology of the Inca people."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Ugaritic Texts"
msgid_plural "copies of the Ugaritic Texts"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Ugaritic Texts"
msgid ""
"A pretty rare English translation of the Ugaritic Texts, a collection of "
"ancient mythological, religious and literature texts regarding the "
"Canaanites.  It contains religious epics such as the Baal Cycle, which "
"recounts the myths surrounding the storm god Baal, as well as hymns, prayers, "
"and rituals that shed light on the religious worldview of the ancient "
"Canaanites and their practices."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Book of Kells"
msgid_plural "copies of the Book of Kells"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Book of Kells"
msgid ""
"A extremely rare English translation of the Book of Kells, a highly decorated "
"and illuminated Celtic manuscript, primarily containing the four Gospels of "
"the New Testament.  This translation mimics perfectly the art and style of "
"the original manuscript, including its elaborate calligraphy, with each "
"letter meticulously designed and adorned with various motifs, including "
"animals, humans, and knotwork patterns."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Book of Leinster"
msgid_plural "copies of the Book of Leister"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Book of Leinster"
msgid ""
"A incredibly rare English translation of the Book of Leinster, a significant "
"and ancient compilation of Irish literature and history, dating back to the "
"12th century.  It contains annals, genealogies, historical texts, legal "
"tracts, secular and religious poetry and stories from Irish mythology, such "
"as the epic tale \"Táin Bó Cúailnge\", which tells the story of the legendary "
"warrior Cú Chulainn and the cattle raid of Cooley."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Mabinogion"
msgid_plural "copies of the Mabinogion"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Mabinogion"
msgid ""
"A rare English translation of the Mabinogion, a collection of twelve medieval "
"Welsh tales, dating back to the 11th and 12th centuries.  It provide a "
"valuable insight into the mythology, history, religion and culture of "
"medieval Wales."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Atra-Hasis"
msgid_plural "copies of the Atra-Hasis"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Atra-Hasis"
msgid ""
"A rare English translation of the Mesopotamian Epic Atra-Hasis.  Named for "
"its protagonist, Atrahasis ('exceedingly wise'), the Atra-Hasis include both "
"a creation myth and one of three surviving Babylonian flood myths."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Enki and Ninhursag Myth"
msgid_plural "copies of the Enki and Ninhursag Myth"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Enki and Ninhursag Myth"
msgid ""
"A pretty uncommon English translation of the Enki and Ninhursag Myth, a "
"Sumerian creation myth that explains the origins of the world, humanity, and "
"the gods."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "The Descent of Inanna"
msgid_plural "copies of The Descent of Inanna"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "The Descent of Inanna"
msgid ""
"A very rare English translation of the Descent of Inanna, an ancient Sumerian "
"myth that recounts the journey of the goddess Inanna into the underworld, "
"where she seeks to confront her sister Ereshkigal, the Queen of the "
"Underworld."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Heliand"
msgid_plural "copies of the Heliand"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Heliand"
msgid ""
"A English translation of the Heliand, an Old Saxon epic poem that narrates "
"the life and passion of Jesus Christ.  It begins with the Annunciation to the "
"Virgin Mary and continues with the birth of Jesus.  It then narrates the "
"story of Jesus' childhood, his baptism by John the Baptist, and his public "
"ministry.  This poem also includes various miracles performed by Jesus, such "
"as healing the sick, raising the dead, and calming the storm."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Item name
msgid "Alphabet of Sirach"
msgid_plural "copies of the Alphabet of Sirach"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/items/book/spiritual.json
#. ~ Description of "Alphabet of Sirach"
msgid ""
"A rare English translation of the Alphabet of Sirach, a compilation of two "
"lists of proverbs, 22 in Jewish Babylonian Aramaic and 22 in Medieval Hebrew "
"(all translated to English), both arranged as alphabetic acrostics, with each "
"proverb followed by an aggadic commentary."
