msgid ""
"An antique double-barreled shotgun chambered in 12 gauge.  Not to be confused "
"with the board game company of the same name, Parker Bros. made shotguns from "
"1867 to 1942, before they were phased out of production by Remington, who had "
"acquired the company the previous decade.  These shotguns were sold in many "
"different \"grades\" at varying price points, with higher quality of "
"engravings being included at higher cost.  This particular shotgun is a "
"\"Trojan\", which was the cheapest grade Parker Bros. sold."
msgstr ""

