msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "scup"
msgid ""
"Also known as porgy, the scup is a small fish commonly found in Atlantic "
"coastal waters, recognizable by its silver body with blue and purple tinges."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "bluefish"
msgid_plural "bluefish"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "bluefish"
msgid ""
"The bluefish, a moderately proportioned marine fish, is known for its "
"aggressive nature and sharp teeth.  It sports a distinct blue-green "
"coloration."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Atlantic cod"
msgid_plural "Atlantic cod"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Atlantic cod"
msgid ""
"A large, white-meat fish known for its mild flavor and flaky texture.  Highly "
"prized in both commercial and recreational fishing."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "haddock"
msgid_plural "haddock"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "haddock"
msgid ""
"A popular food fish, the haddock is recognized by its dark lateral line and a "
"black blotch above the pectoral fin."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Atlantic bluefin tuna"
msgid_plural "Atlantic bluefin tuna"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Atlantic bluefin tuna"
msgid ""
"One of the largest and fastest fish in the waters of New England, the bluefin "
"tuna is a streamlined predator with a dark blue back and silvery sides."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "Atlantic halibut"
msgid_plural "Atlantic halibut"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "Atlantic halibut"
msgid ""
"The largest flatfish in the ocean, known for its dense, firm texture and mild "
"flavor."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "pollock"
msgid_plural "pollock"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""
msgstr[3] ""

#: data/json/monsters/fish.json
#. ~ Description of monster "pollock"
msgid ""
"A member of the cod family, pollock is a versatile fish known for its white, "
"delicate meat and mild taste."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "fungal blossom"
msgid_plural "fungal blossoms"
msgstr[0] "grzybiczy kwiat"
msgstr[1] "grzybicze kwiaty"
msgstr[2] "grzybiczych kwiatów"
msgstr[3] "grzybiczego kwiatu"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "fungal blossom"
msgid ""
"A broad fungus, looking much like a glowing blue sunflower.  It appears to "
"emit finer spores than the typical fungal emission."
msgstr ""
"Rozłożysty grzyb, bardzo przypominający świecący niebieski słonecznik. "
"Wygląda na to, że rozprzestrzenia zarodniki drobniejsze w porównaniu do "
"typowych grzybiczych emisji."

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Monster name
msgid "fungal hedgerow"
msgid_plural "fungal hedgerows"
msgstr[0] "grzybiczy żywopłot"
msgstr[1] "grzybicze żywopłoty"
msgstr[2] "grzybiczych żywopłotów"
msgstr[3] "grzybiczego żywopłotu"

#: data/json/monsters/fungus.json
#. ~ Description of monster "fungal hedgerow"
msgid ""
"Looking at first glance like a dull gray privet, this \"hedge\" is really a "
"mass of barbed fungal tendrils, defending the fungal tower."
msgstr ""
"Wyglądający na pierwszy rzut oka na nudny szary ligustr, ten „żywopłot” jest "
"w rzeczywistości masą ciernistych grzybiczych splotów chroniących grzybiczą "
"wieżę."

