#: data/json/npcs/exodii/non-NPC_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Follow the directions on the pictographic sign"
msgstr "Postępuj zgodnie z instrukcjami podanymi na znaku piktograficznym"

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/non-NPC_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Follow the directions on the pictographic sign"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Follow the directions on the pictographic sign"
msgid ""
"I found a weird pictographic sign that seemed to point towards someone "
"willing to trade."
msgstr ""
"Znalazłem dziwny piktograficzny znak, który wskazywał na kogoś chętnego do "
"handlu."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/non-NPC_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Follow the directions on the pictographic sign"
msgid ""
"This is a sign with a series of simple line-art pictograms showing what "
"appears to be a basic trade transaction.  A pair of hands offers a piece of "
"some kind of junk, and another pair of hands offers a small pouch in return."
msgstr ""
"Jest to znak z serią prostych piktogramów przedstawiających coś, co wydaje "
"się być podstawową transakcją handlową. Para rąk oferuje kawałek jakiegoś "
"złomu, a inna para rąk oferuje w zamian małą sakiewkę."

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/alphatest_dialogue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"[v0.1 info] Okay I'm just gonna drop my dialect for this, it's way too much "
"for Anglic.  The Labyrinthine Structure (LS) is planned to be a sprawling "
"procedurally generated dungeon where you can fight advanced monsters and loot "
"cybernetics, both regular and weird artifact versions.  It is currently far "
"from that state.  Playtest information on the general layout and the monster "
"balance would be helpful.\n"
"\n"
"In the long run, the goal is to have a number of 'biomes' that you can reach "
"as you travel further from the origin point.  When you leave and return, the "
"dungeon resets, although in the future the devs want to have a stable 'home "
"base' you can upgrade.\n"
"\n"
"In its final form, if it ever gets there, it would have enough content that "
"you could spend an entire playthrough just exploring the labyrinth and "
"getting weird unique items that only work down there, something like the "
"backrooms mod but for mainline."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/alphatest_dialogue.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's stop breaking the fourth wall and get back to the normal conversation."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/exodii/netherum/labyrinth_computers.json
