#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
msgid "logger"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_employees.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
msgid "manager"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_employees.json
#. ~ Job description of "Lumberjack" NPC class
msgid "I felled trees before the apocalypse.  Zombies shouldn't be as tough."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find Drive Belts"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find Drive Belts"
msgid "Obtain 3 drive belts in exchange for credit with the loggers."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
msgid "I need three drive belts."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
msgid ""
"Some of our machinery received some damage before <the_cataclysm> and we were "
"waiting on replacement parts.  Now everything's changed and those parts are "
"more important than ever.  Get us three drive belts and I'll give you some "
"credit with us."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Magnetrons"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 100 Solder"
msgid "Someone's got to do it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
msgid ""
"If you can't find actual drive belts on engines, a good replacement can be "
"made from a belt and some duct tape.  Nothing difficult."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
msgid "Do you have the belts?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
msgid "Wonderful!  Thanks, <name_g>, we'll be fine for a long while from now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 25 Magnetrons"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 300 Charcoal"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Obtain 100 Solder"
msgid "Where are they?  I don't believe you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Drive Belts"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 6 Blankets"
msgid "That's unfortunate.  I guess we'll have to find someone else to do it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Get 1,000 Nails"
msgstr "Zdobądź 1000 gwoździ"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
msgid "Obtain 1,000 nails in exchange for credit with the loggers."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
msgid "I need 1,000 nails."
msgstr "Potrzebuję 1000 gwoździ."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
msgid ""
"Along with those drive belts, we were waiting for some nails for structural "
"repairs.  Due to <the_cataclysm>, we obviously never received them.  So, I "
"need you to get us 1,000 nails.  We'll pay you fairly."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
msgid "Taking apart some furniture in town should get what you need."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
msgid "Do you have the nails?"
msgstr "Masz już te gwoździe?"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 1,000 Nails"
msgid "Our warehouse was about to fall apart.  These will be extremely helpful to us."
msgstr ""
"Mało brakowało a nasz magazyn rozpadłby się na kawałki. Bardzo się nam "
"przysłużyłeś."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Get 6,800 Nails"
msgstr "Zdobądź 6800 gwoździ"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
msgid "Obtain 6,800 nails in exchange for credit with the loggers."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
msgid "I need 6,800 nails."
msgstr "Potrzebuję 6800 gwoździ."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
msgid ""
"While fairly sturdy, the metal fence around this place won't hold out for "
"long.  So, we've decided to replace it with a wall.  However, the nails we "
"had were used to repair our existing structures, and they weren't nearly "
"enough.  After some calculations, we need 6,800 nails to do it.  That may "
"seem like a lot, but we're willing to give you a TON of credit for it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
msgid "Well, I suppose that's reasonable."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
msgid ""
"You might have to do more than just scrapping a bunch of furniture.  "
"Dismantling a building somewhere in town could get you what you need."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
msgid "That's absolutely amazing!  I can't thank you enough for this!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get 6,800 Nails"
msgid "You're a fucking scammer, <name_b>!"
msgstr "Jesteś pieprzonym oszustem, <name_b>!"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find 6 Blankets"
msgstr "Znajdź 6 koców"

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find 6 Blankets"
msgid "Obtain 6 blankets or quilts in exchange for credit with the loggers."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 6 Blankets"
msgid "I need 6 blankets."
msgstr "Potrzebuję 6 koców."

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 6 Blankets"
msgid ""
"Now that we should be safe from harm, I decided to start adding a few things "
"to this place.  Right now, we don't have anywhere to comfortably sleep, so "
"we're building a small sleeping quarter.  We just need 6 big, warm blankets "
"or quilts to finish our project."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 6 Blankets"
msgid "I figure any hotel or motel in town should have lots of blankets."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 6 Blankets"
msgid "Did you find us some bedding yet?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 6 Blankets"
msgid ""
"Thanks!  Feel free to sleep here if you want.  It's the least we can do for "
"the help."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find 6 Blankets"
msgid "How is this supposed to help us?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid ""
"Establish trade relations between the loggers and a refugee center, and bring "
"back a writ of the agreement."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid ""
"While some of us were out scavenging, we spotted an old evac shelter that "
"looks like it might have some people inside.  I want you to go over there, "
"find whoever runs the joint, and see if we can make a deal with them for some "
"processed lumber.  This will be invaluable to our survival."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid "Please give it a try?  This is really important to us."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid "What did they say about the deal?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid "Thank you!  We're set for life on this one!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid "How does this help us?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/lumbermill_employees/lumbermill_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Establish A Trade Route"
msgid "That's unfortunate.  I guess we'll have to find someone else to trade with."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Guard.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ A member of the Gray Moose Lodge, trying to safe in their isolated
#. location
msgid "Militia Guard"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Guard.json
#. ~ Job description of "Guard" NPC class
msgid "I'm a local guard."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Guard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm busy on watch duty.  Talk to the Boss upstairs."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Guard.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm on watch duty.  Talk to the Boss.  He's upstairs."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Guard.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Stay safe out there.  Hate to have to kill you after you've already died."
msgstr ""
"Bądź bezpieczny tam na zewnątrz. Wolałbym cię nie zabijać po tym jak już i "
"tak będziesz martwy."

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
#. ~ A member of the Gray Moose Militia, trying to safe in their isolated
#. location
msgid "Darby Sutton"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Welcome to our camp.  Behave yourself while you are here.  What can I do for "
"you?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/npcs/Salvor_Market/uica_vehicle_marchant_talk.json
#: data/mods/aftershock_exoplanet/npcs/Salvor_Market/uica_vehicle_marchant_talk.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you do here?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's the story behind this place?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Time for me to leave"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm the most senior member at this point so I'm what passes for the leader "
"here now.  I'm just trying to make plans to keep us alive since everything "
"fell apart."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, that's a long story.  We are what's left of the Grey Moose militia.  We "
"had plans for when things went south cause of crazy politicians or war, but "
"we didn't expect people to go crazy then turn zombie.  Only a handful of our "
"members actually made it through all that madness.  What's worse is that we "
"lost so much of our supplies and gear due to military checkpoints and trigger "
"happy soldiers.  It didn't matter that half of us were former military the "
"checkpoint guards just saw weapons, panicked and then confiscated everything "
"but the clothes on our back.  So here we are at our planned escape location "
"with not even a fraction of our manpower or supplies."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I can't say I can think of anything at the moment.  Our remoteness is our "
"defense.  We want to keep a low profile and try to keep out of any trouble in "
"this isolated location.  We are willing to trade for weapons and ammo though. "
" Keeping the nearby area clear and hunting is always eating away at our "
"supplies."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Keeping a low profile is good."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/militia/GM_Militia_Merchant.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Stay safe out there.  Not enough of us are around anymore."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Former miner, poor fellow succumbed to spiral madness.
msgid "miner"
msgstr "Górnik"

#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
msgid "Miner"
msgstr "Górnik"

#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
#. ~ Job description of "Miner" NPC class
msgid "Spirals."
msgstr "Spirale."

#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Spirals?"
msgstr "Spirale?"

#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hello there!"
msgstr "Witajcie."

#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm outta here.  Bye."
msgstr "Znikam stąd. Żegnam."

#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Poor fellow - looks like you're out of your mind.  Can't help you, sorry.  "
"I'm outta here.  Bye."
msgstr ""
"Biedny facet - wygląda na to, że postradałeś zmysły. Nie mogę ci pomóc, "
"przykro mi. Spadam stąd. Żegnaj."

#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry, what?"
msgstr "Przepraszam, co?"

#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why are you repeating 'spirals' over and over again?"
msgstr "Czemu powtarzasz „spirale” jak nakręcony?"

#: data/json/npcs/mine/spiral_madman.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are you nuts?"
msgstr "Odbiło ci?"

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_Soldier_1.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/NPC_Old_Guard_RED_Soldier_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm afraid I can't talk now."
msgstr "Obawiam się, że nie mogę teraz rozmawiać."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_Soldier_1.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/NPC_Old_Guard_RED_Soldier_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Stay safe out there."
msgstr "Miej się na baczności."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_Soldier_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Welcome to camp Arabella"
msgstr "Witaj w obozie Arabella"

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_Soldier_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm supposed to direct all questions to my leadership."
msgstr "Mam polecenie odsyłać wszelkie pytania do mojego dowództwa."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_Soldier_1.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "If you're looking to trade you'll need to talk to the quartermaster."
msgstr "Jeśli chcesz pohandlować, musisz porozmawiać z kwatermistrzem."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Generic guard for the old guard.
msgid "Duhring"
msgstr "Duhring"

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
#. ~ Generic guard for the old guard.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
msgid "Officer"
msgstr "Oficer"

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#. ~ Job description of "Officer" NPC class
msgid "I'm an officer for FOB Arabella"
msgstr "Jestem oficerem FOB Arabella"

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't have any use for you right now.  You will be informed if I need you, "
"soldier."
msgstr ""
"Nie mam dla ciebie zadania. Poinformujemy cię, jeśli będziemy cię "
"potrzebować, żołnierzu."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you tell me about yourself?"
msgstr "Możesz mi opowiedzieć o sobie?"

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/snippets/talk_tags_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ Snippet in category "<acknowledged>"
#. ~ Generic acknowledgment of a command.
msgid "Understood."
msgstr "Zrozumiano."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "If it wasn't clear, you are dismissed soldier."
msgstr "Jeśli to nie było jasne, jesteś oddalony żołnierzu."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I am clearly busy, soldier."
msgstr "Jestem zajęty żołnierzu."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I just ask you some questions?"
msgstr "Mogę tylko zadać ci kilka pytań?"

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Go. Away."
msgstr "Idź sobie."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_officer.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "If I have to tell you one more time so help me god…"
msgstr "Jeśli jeszcze raz mam to ci powtórzyć, to boże…"

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_pilot.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Generic guard for the old guard.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
msgid "Pilot"
msgstr "Pilot"

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_pilot.json
#. ~ Job description of "Pilot" NPC class
msgid "I'm a pilot."
msgstr "Jestem pilotem."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_quartermaster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Welcome to camp Arabella, What will it be?"
msgstr "Witaj w obozie Arabella. Czym mogę służyć?"

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_quartermaster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm the camp quartermaster.  Come and see me if you have anything valuable to "
"trade."
msgstr ""
"Jestem obozowym kwatermistrzem. Przyjdź do mnie, jeśli masz coś wartościowego "
"na wymianę."

#: data/json/npcs/old_guard/NPC_Old_Guard_FOB_quartermaster.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "If you're looking to trade you've come to the right place."
msgstr "Jeśli chcesz się wymienić, jesteś we właściwym miejscu."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
msgid "pizzaiolo"
msgstr "Pizzaiolo"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I got the cake.  Shall we move, <name_g>?"
msgstr "Mam ciasto. Idziemy, <name_g>?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "If you still want to travel with me, let's go."
msgstr "Jeśli nadal chcesz ze mną podróżować, to w drogę."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Lead the way, <name_g>."
msgstr "Prowadź, <name_g>."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Are we there yet, my <name_g>?"
msgstr "Daleko jeszcze, mój <name_g>?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We're here, <name_g>.  Let's celebrate."
msgstr "Dotarliśmy, <name_g>. Świętujmy."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Be patient.  We'll be there soon, <name_g>"
msgstr "Cierpliwości. Wkrótce tam będziemy, <name_g>"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "[*NOM-NOM*]"
msgstr "[*NOM-NOM*]"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Mmm, delicious.  You know, you are good friend, and a good cook.  I'm glad "
"that I'm with you at the day like this.  Say, what do you think about me "
"going with you?  As you can see, my restaurant is thrashes, my house ruined, "
"the only option left is to travel somewhere, and it's better if I do it with "
"someone."
msgstr ""
"Mmm, pychota. Wiesz, jesteś dobrym przyjacielem i dobrym kucharzem. Cieszę "
"się, że jestem z tobą w taki dzień. Powiedz, co myślisz o tym, żebym poszedł "
"z tobą? Jak widzisz, moja restauracja jest rozwalona, mój dom zrujnowany, "
"jedyna opcja jaka mi pozostała to podróżować gdzieś, a lepiej jeśli zrobię to "
"z kimś."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure, <name_g>.  <end_talking>"
msgstr "Pewnie, <name_g>. <end_talking>"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Angry pizzaiolo"
msgstr "Gniewny mistrz pizzy"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Angry pizzaiolo"
msgid ""
"Bring the pizzaiolo to <color_light_blue>their rival's house</color> and "
"don't forget to <color_yellow>bring at least 200 units of gasoline</color>.  "
"After you got there, talk to the pizzaiolo to start burning the house."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Angry pizzaiolo"
msgid ""
"I'm so angry!  I have an enemy that ruined my life, and I want revenge for "
"it!  I don't care about <the_cataclysm>, I just want to burn his <freaking> "
"restaurant!  Will you help me?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Angry pizzaiolo"
msgid ""
"Good.  Let's go to his restaurant and fucking burn it!  Oh, by the way, could "
"you bring gasoline with you, <name_g>?  I was so angry I forgot to bring it "
"with me…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Angry pizzaiolo"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find TrueFoodperson"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pizza parlor"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Family house"
msgid "What?!  Why do you… ah, forget it."
msgstr "Co?! Dlaczego ty… ach, zapomnij o tym."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Angry pizzaiolo"
msgid "Maybe we can find some gasoline at gas station."
msgstr "Może znajdziemy trochę paliwa na stacji benzynowej."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Angry pizzaiolo"
msgid ""
"Sweet, sweet revenge!  It smells so nice!  His restaurant burns, his legacy "
"is now ruined!  Even if he became a <zombie>, it still good."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find TrueFoodperson"
msgstr "Znajdź TrueFoodperson"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find TrueFoodperson"
msgid "Help pizzaiolo find TrueFoodperson and kick his ass."
msgstr "Pomóż mistrzowi pizzy znaleźć TrueFoodperson i skopać mu tyłek."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find TrueFoodperson"
msgid ""
"Ah, it's you, <name_g>.  Wanna continue on my revenge to all American "
"<name_b>s?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find TrueFoodperson"
msgid ""
"Good.  Next stop, Foodplace.  I always hated that place, especially that "
"<freaking> <name_b> in his idiotic mask.  I know he's still alive, hiding in "
"his dumb parody of a restaurant.  Take this bat.  Let's take a visit to him, "
"<name_g>, and kick his <freaking> ass!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find TrueFoodperson"
msgid ""
"I heard that these 'restaurants' use some kind of locking system for staff "
"room, so we would need to find a way to get there."
msgstr ""
"Słyszałem, że te „restauracje” używają jakiegoś systemu zamykania pomieszczeń "
"dla personelu, więc musielibyśmy znaleźć sposób, aby się tam dostać."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find TrueFoodperson"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pizza parlor"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Family house"
msgid "I'm waiting."
msgstr "Czekam."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find TrueFoodperson"
msgid "Another one bite the dust!  We did good, <name_g>."
msgstr "Kolejny gryzie piach! Dobrze nam poszło, <name_g>."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Pizza parlor"
msgstr "Pizzeria"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Pizza parlor"
msgid "Help pizzaiolo take back his restaurant."
msgstr "Pomóż mistrzowi pizzy odzyskać jego restaurację."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pizza parlor"
msgid ""
"I need to make a last step to achieve my revenge, and the step is - my pizza "
"parlor.  Before <the_cataclysm>, the bank took my place, and now, some "
"<freaking> <name_b>s occupied it and made it their base!  Just unbelievable, "
"I tell ya.  It's time for me to fight back, deal with this <freaking> "
"<name_b>s and regain my honor.  Are you with me, <name_g>?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pizza parlor"
msgid "Very good.  <lets_go>"
msgstr "Bardzo dobrze.  <lets_go>"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pizza parlor"
msgid "These <name_b>s might be heavily armed, so we need to prepare to face them."
msgstr ""
"Ci <name_b> mogą być silnie uzbrojeni, więc musimy się przygotować na "
"stawienie im czoła."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Pizza parlor"
msgid ""
"Nice, very fucking nice.  Fuck, this placed is thrashed.  <freaking> "
"<name_b>s thrashed my restaurant!  Okay, calm down, calm down, will ya… At "
"least I retrieved my place.  Thank you, <name_g>.  I couldn't make it without "
"you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Family house"
msgstr "Dom rodzinny"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Family house"
msgid "First bring pizzaiolo some chocolate cake then lead him to his family house."
msgstr ""
"Najpierw przynieś mistrzowi pizzy ciasto czekoladowe, a następnie zaprowadź "
"go do jego rodzinnego domu."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Family house"
msgid ""
"Now, as my competitors dead, their places are ruined, it's time to relax… I "
"know, let's celebrate it!  Lead me to my house.  Also, we need a cake for "
"that.  What celebration without a cake, right?  I can teach you how to cook "
"it, if you want."
msgstr ""
"Teraz, kiedy moi konkurenci nie żyją, ich miejsca są zrujnowane, nadszedł "
"czas na relaks… Wiem, uczcijmy to! Zabierz mnie do mojego domu. Do tego "
"potrzebujemy tortu. Co to za święto bez tortu, prawda? Mogę cię nauczyć jak "
"go upiec, jeśli chcesz."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Family house"
msgid "Good.  Bring me chocolate cake and talk to me."
msgstr "Dobrze. Przynieś mi ciasto czekoladowe to pogadamy."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Family house"
msgid ""
"If you listened to me very closely, it wouldn't be hard for you to make it.  "
"Good luck, <name_g>."
msgstr ""
"Jeśli słuchałeś mnie bardzo uważnie, nie byłoby to dla Ciebie trudne do "
"wykonania. Powodzenia, <name_g>."

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Player message in an effect
msgid "You learn how to craft cake."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Are we there yet, <name_g>?  I can't wait to burn that building!"
msgstr "Daleko jeszcze, <name_g>? Nie mogę się doczekać, aż spalę tę budę!"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#: data/mods/innawood/npcs/missiondef.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We're here.  Let's do it!"
msgstr "Jesteśmy. Bierzmy się za to!"

#: data/json/npcs/other/NPC_pizzaiolo.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Be patient, <name_g>, we're getting there soon."
msgstr "Cierpliwości, <name_g>, wkrótce tam dotrzemy."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Finally, someone who isn't part of those <zombies>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Yeah, today's your lucky day.  Hand over your stuff, or you'll be one "
"yourself."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, nice to meet you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_CAMPER.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<greet>"
msgstr "<greet>"

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Who are you, exactly?"
msgstr "Kim właściwie jesteś?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Wanna buy something, maybe sell off what you don't need?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could I buy one of your pets?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's quite noble of you, but how do you take care of so many animals?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"To be honest with you, it's been pretty difficult.  I sneak out at night or "
"whenever there's an opening to grab whatever I need and come back before "
"something notices me.  I've been held up for quite a while whenever a horde "
"decides to pass by.  Good thing we had some spare bookcases lying around, or "
"I'd be a goner by now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_hunter.json
#: data/json/npcs/robofac/robofac_intercom/robofac_intercom_prototypes.json
#: data/json/npcs/scrap_trader/scrap_trader.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_scrapper.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/NC_Yoshimi.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Interesting."
msgstr "Interesujące."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I hate to see them go, but I think you'd be able to take better care of one "
"than I can right now.  I can sell you a cat or dog of your choosing, for $25 "
"and $50, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've changed my mind, let's talk about something else."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have a dog."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have a cat."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#: data/mods/Defense_Mode/dialogue/TALK_WANDERING_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hand over your stuff!  Don't make any sudden moves, or you die!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "What brings you around here?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Would you be interested in trading at all?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I stay here for a while?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_CAMPER.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_shelter_survivors.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why don't you come with me?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why would someone leave a gun store open in all this chaos?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, they weren't really around to lock it up.  Whoever got here first blew "
"their head off with a 12-gauge, but they were up and movin', tried to kill me "
"too.  They're out in the dumpster now."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_GUN_STORE_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry to hear that.  Maybe we should change the subject."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/mods/Defense_Mode/dialogue/TALK_WANDERING_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Freeze you <freaking> <zombies>!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/mods/Defense_Mode/dialogue/TALK_WANDERING_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "&Hold up your hands.  \"Don't worry, I'm not going to hurt you\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What are you doing in this deathtrap?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_APARTMENT_SURVIVOR.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_CAMPER.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_shelter_survivors.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Wow."
msgstr "Wow."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_CAMPER.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_shelter_survivors.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "<greet>."
msgstr "<greet>."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_CAMPER.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Glad to see you too.  Now, hand over your things."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/TALK_TECHNO_KID.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey <name_g>."
msgstr "Hej <name_g>."

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just wandering, <name_g>."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'll make this real simple for you.  Hand over your stuff, and no one gets "
"hurt, capiche?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I purchase any of your liquor?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It's a bit dangerous to be out here alone.  Why don't you come with me?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_MOONSHINER.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Anything I could do for you?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Would you be interested in bartering?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_NPC_PREPPER_SURVIVOR.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I guess you could borrow one of the spare beds, just don't hog it.  I "
"kept a few in case someone else joined me, but no one I knew came here."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_shelter_survivors.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Don't come any closer!"
msgstr "Nie zbliżaj się!"

#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_shelter_survivors.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_sickly_laborer.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's wrong?"
msgstr "Co się stało?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/camp_start.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's stay here, then.  I trust your decisions."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
msgid "meteorologist"
msgstr "Meteorolog"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
msgid "Meteorologist"
msgstr "Meteorolog"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Job description of "Meteorologist" NPC class
msgid "Meteorologist."
msgstr "Meteorolog."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Run, I need to run, where to run…"
msgstr "Uciekać, muszę uciekać, gdzie uciekać…"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Maybe I can help you with your problem?"
msgstr "Może mogę pomóc ci z twoim problemem?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I need more time.  Come back later."
msgstr "Potrzebuję więcej czasu. Przyjdź później."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#: data/json/npcs/snippets/talk_tags_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ Snippet in category "<acknowledged>"
#. ~ Generic acknowledgment of a command.
msgid "No problem."
msgstr "Żaden problem."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yes, you can relax now."
msgstr "Tak, możesz teraz odpocząć."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Don't worry, we're getting there soon."
msgstr "Nie martw się, wkrótce tam dotrzemy."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Thank you.  I will never forget your kindness, <name_g>.  Take this book as "
"token of my gratitude."
msgstr ""
"Dziękuję. Nigdy nie zapomnę twojej dobroci, <name_g>. Przyjmij tę książkę "
"jako dowód mojej wdzięczności."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Me too."
msgstr "Ja też."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
msgstr "Znajdź złom dla meteorologa"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
msgid "The meteorologist asked to bring him 50 pieces of scrap."
msgstr "Meteorolog poprosił o przyniesienie mu 50 kawałków złomu."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
msgid "We need scrap metal to assemble a drone…"
msgstr "Potrzebujemy metalowy złom do złożenia drona…"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
msgid ""
"I've been sitting here for a long time, and all that time I was wondering how "
"bad everything is outside.  I want to build a drone that I can use to fly "
"over New England, check the air condition, take a few pictures from above to "
"get a glimpse of how is it.  There were a lot of things in our back room that "
"could be useful, but still I'm missing a lot of things.  You look like an "
"experienced survivalist.  Can you help me?"
msgstr ""
"Siedzę tu od dłuższego czasu i przez cały ten czas zastanawiałem się, jak źle "
"jest na zewnątrz. Chcę zbudować drona, którym będę mógł latać nad Nową "
"Anglią, sprawdzać stan powietrza, zrobić kilka zdjęć z góry, żeby zorientować "
"się, jak jest. Na naszym zapleczu było wiele rzeczy, które mogłyby się "
"przydać, ale wciąż brakuje mi wielu rzeczy. Wyglądasz na doświadczonego "
"survivalowca. Czy możesz mi pomóc?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
msgid ""
"Good.  I just need a little stuff: 50 scrap, 6 medium batteries, 5 small "
"high-quality lenses and a radio remote control.  Bring the scrap for now, but "
"don't forget about the rest."
msgstr ""
"Dobrze. Potrzebuję tylko trochę rzeczy: 50 sztuk złomu, 6 średnich baterii, 5 "
"małych obiektywów wysokiej jakości i zdalnego sterowania radiowego. Przynieś "
"na razie złom, ale nie zapomnij o reszcie."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_barber.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Maybe another time…"
msgstr "Może innym razem…"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
msgid ""
"I don't think this is a difficult task.  Surely there is a lot of it "
"underfoot."
msgstr ""
"Nie sądzę żeby to było trudne zadanie. Z pewnością jest tego wiele pod "
"stopami."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
msgid "How's it going?"
msgstr "Jak leci?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
msgid "Great, I'm starting to work on it…"
msgstr "Świetnie, no to rozpoczynam nad nim pracę…"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find scrap for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
msgid "Why do you say that?"
msgstr "Czemu tak mówisz?"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
msgstr "Znajdź baterie dla meteorologa"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
msgid "The meteorologist asked to bring him 6 medium batteries."
msgstr "Meteorolog poprosił o przyniesienie mu 6 średnich baterii."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
msgid "We need batteries to assemble a drone…"
msgstr "Potrzebujemy baterii do złożenia drona…"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
msgid ""
"Well, what's next on the list… yeah, batteries.  6 medium batteries would be "
"enough."
msgstr ""
"Cóż, co jest następne na liście… tak, baterie. 6 średnich baterii by "
"wystarczyło."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
msgid "I'm waiting for you."
msgstr "Czekam na ciebie."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
msgid "Try looking for some battery-powered trinkets and take them apart."
msgstr ""
"Spróbuj poszukać jakichś gadżetów zasilanych bateriami i rozbierz je na "
"części."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find batteries for the meteorologist"
msgid "Great, I'm continue to work on it…"
msgstr "Świetnie, no to kontynuuję nad nim pracę…"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
msgid "The meteorologist asked to bring him 5 small high-quality lenses."
msgstr "Meteorolog poprosił o przyniesienie mu 5 małych soczewek wysokiej jakości."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
msgid "We need small high quality lenses for our drone…"
msgstr "Potrzebujemy małych, wysokiej jakości soczewek do naszego drona…"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
msgid ""
"Well, what's next on the list… yeah, lenses.  5 small high-quality lenses "
"would be enough."
msgstr ""
"Cóż, co jest następne na liście… tak, soczewki. 5 małych soczewek wysokiej "
"jakości by wystarczyło."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
msgid "Try looking for telescopes or microscopes to dismantle."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find high-quality lenses for the meteorologist"
msgid "Great, I'm continuing to work on it…"
msgstr "Świetnie, no to kontynuuję nad nim pracę…"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
msgid "The meteorologist asked to bring him a radio controller."
msgstr "Meteorolog poprosił o przyniesienie mu radiowy sterownik."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
msgid "We need an RC to assemble a drone…"
msgstr "Potrzebujemy sterowania radiowego do złożenia drona…"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
msgid ""
"Well, what's next on the list… yeah, radio control.  Any kind will do, but "
"the simplest one is better, so I can easily reconfigure it for my drone."
msgstr ""
"Cóż, co jest następne na liście… tak, sterowanie radiowe. Każdy rodzaj się "
"nada, ale najprostszy jest lepszy, żebym mógł go łatwo przekonfigurować do "
"mojego drona."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
msgid "I advise you to search in a store, such as electronics or toy store."
msgstr "Radzę poszukać w sklepie, np. z elektroniką lub zabawkami."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a radio controller for the meteorologist"
msgid ""
"Great, very little work left.  I need a few days to finish all this, and to "
"try it in work.  I hope everything will work fine!  While I'm working on the "
"drone, you can read this book.  Maybe you can learn something new from it."
msgstr ""
"Świetnie, zostało niewiele pracy. Potrzebuję kilku dni, żeby to wszystko "
"skończyć i wypróbować w praktyce. Mam nadzieję, że wszystko będzie działać "
"dobrze! Podczas gdy ja będę pracował nad dronem, Ty możesz poczytać tę "
"książkę. Może dowiesz się z niej czegoś nowego."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
msgid "The meteorologist asked to bring him his crashed drone."
msgstr "Meteorolog poprosił o przyniesienie mu jego rozbitego drona."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
msgid "I've lost the drone, we should find out what happened…"
msgstr "Straciłem drona, powinniśmy się dowiedzieć, co się stało…"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
msgid ""
"I'm glad that you are alive and that you haven't forgot about me.  The drone "
"turned out to be great, it managed to take off and even was able to fly "
"several hundred meters!  Unfortunately, after that, I lost control of it… I "
"don't know what happened to it, though.  Maybe you can check?  I'm a little "
"afraid to go out there…"
msgstr ""
"Cieszę się, że żyjesz i że o mnie nie zapomniałeś. Dron okazał się świetny, "
"udało mu się wystartować i nawet był w stanie przelecieć kilkaset metrów! "
"Niestety, potem straciłem nad nim kontrolę… Nie wiem jednak, co się z nim "
"stało. Może mógłbyś sprawdzić? Trochę się boję tam wychodzić…"

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
msgid ""
"I don't know quite what happened.  Maybe something noticed my drone and tried "
"to bring it down.  Be careful."
msgstr ""
"Nie wiem do końca, co się stało. Może coś zauważyło mojego drona i próbowało "
"go strącić. Uważaj."

#: data/json/npcs/other/meteorologist.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the meteorologist's crashed drone"
msgid ""
"Hmm, I see that the drone is not with you.  Maybe at least the memory module "
"remains?  Okay, show it to me… hmm, situation is worse than I expected, much, "
"much worse… I'm not feeling good.  I don't feel safe in this place anymore.  "
"I have to run, run somewhere.  But where to run if these monsters are "
"everywhere…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Nothing to it.  Before <the_cataclysm>, it didn't take much to find yourself "
"here.  And I guess it just made sense to stay.  We seem to be doing better "
"than most, anyway."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/TALK_homeless_survivor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Surviving, as I always have.  Is that what you mean?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Who are you?  Would you like to trade?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where might your friends be?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I stay here?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I purchase some of your wares?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How's that smoker coming along?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Making ends meet, even in the worst circumstances.  We've been camping out "
"here now, trading with whoever passes by.  If something catches your eye, let "
"me know."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We got tired of being out on the road and decided to stay here for a bit.  "
"We've found a lot of useful stuff out and about, so if you see anything you "
"need I'll make you a deal."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"They should be around here somewhere.  We usually go out in teams to "
"scavenge, and they haven't told me about anything yet.  They might have "
"something for you to do."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I don't see anything wrong with it.  We should have a spare bed in that "
"tent you could sleep on.  Just don't cause any trouble."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure!  It turned out well enough for us, and it's one of the few fresh meats "
"we can find.  I'll pay fairly for it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I have nothing."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I have nothing.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's wonderful!  We've been preserving a lot more of what we manage to "
"scavenge so we won't have to worry about our food going bad for a while.  "
"We'd be willing to sell some of the excess, if you want."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I think I'll buy 10 slices.  [$20]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You think 20 slices would be alright?  [$40]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_broker.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll take 50 slices of the stuff.  [$100]"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Who are you, and what are you doing here?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you.  I mean no harm."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's with that guy in the tent?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Want to trade?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, they're right over there, and one of us is in that tent over there.  They "
"handle any stuff we manage to scavenge, so feel free to trade for what you "
"want."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Thanks for the offer, but I don't have anything to spare right now.  One of "
"my buddies over in that tent handles stuff like this, though.  You might find "
"something."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/TALK_homeless_group_survivors.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, they were the brightest of us when all hell broke loose.  They managed "
"to get us some food and weapons early on.  I guess that just kinda made them "
"the leader."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Sticky Situation"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Sticky Situation"
msgid ""
"Kill some slimes in exchange for credit with some of the traders and bring "
"back six of their slime scraps."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgid "I need some help."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
msgid ""
"We've had some trouble with slimes not far from us.  It's been hard going "
"through there with all them around, so I want you to go take care of it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
msgid "I'll be here when you get back."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
msgid "No problem.  I'm sure one of us will get to it anyway."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
msgid ""
"Sure, they can be cut, but I'd say it's better to splatter them with "
"something large and heavy."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
msgid "Are those slimes dead yet?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
msgid ""
"Nice.  I'll just take those off your hands.  Might be good for greasing the "
"bike chains and door hinges around here even though it is a bit… abnormal."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
msgid "You don't look nearly as sticky as you're supposed to.  Get back to it."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Sticky Situation"
msgid "Did they give you the slip?  It's worse than I thought, then."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Arthropod Hunting"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Arthropod Hunting"
msgid ""
"Kill some ants and bring back ten slices of their meat in exchange for credit "
"with some of the traders."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
msgid ""
"The last time we went out scouting we found some gargantuan ants crawling "
"around.  We thought we might see how they taste, if they could be cooked and "
"whatnot.  I want you to go kill one and bring back some of its meat."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
msgid "Alright, I can understand that."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
msgid "A shotgun of some sort might work well."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
msgid "Do you have the meat?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
msgid ""
"Nice.  I'll get these cooked up.  Who knows, we might want some more in the "
"future."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
msgid "You sure?  I don't see my meat anywhere."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Arthropod Hunting"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgid "Ah, well.  It's no big deal."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Refurbishments"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Refurbishments"
msgid "Obtain 100 planks."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
msgid ""
"My buddies and I have decided to stay here for a while.  This is about the "
"only safe place out here, and it's kinda become our home.  Anyway, we're "
"going to build a wall.  Our old logs have provided a bunch of the wood, but "
"we still need quite a few planks.  About 100 of them.  If you could get it "
"for us, I'd be grateful."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgid "Thank you.  We'll be sure to compensate your efforts."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgid "Alright, I can understand that.  I guess I'll have to get it myself."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
msgid ""
"Any nearby forest should have all you need.  Otherwise, you might try "
"breaking down some furniture in town."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
msgid "Do you have my lumber?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
msgid "Thank you.  We'll start right away."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgid "I can tell you're lying.  I don't see shit."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Refurbishments Pt. II"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
msgid "Obtain 150 planks."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. II"
msgid ""
"Now that we've got the wall done, we decided to move out of these old tents.  "
"We still have some leftover nails but we need more wood.  So, if you could "
"get us 150 planks, we'd be grateful."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Refurbishments Pt. III"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
msgid "Obtain 6 ropes."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
msgid ""
"Our entrance is wide open so we're building a gate over it.  Problem is we "
"don't have any ropes.  If you could find some for us, we'll pay you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
msgid ""
"If you can't find any rope around, one of our books should have something on "
"rope-making.  Most plants can be woven into a halfway decent rope."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. III"
msgid "Do you have my ropes?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
msgid "Obtain a wood saw."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
msgid ""
"We appreciate all of your help but we can't rely on everyone else to do "
"things for us.  I'd be willing to buy a wood saw of some kind from you so we "
"can cut our own wood as needed."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
msgid "A hardware store or lumbermill should have one."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
msgid "Do you have my saw?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. IV"
msgid "Thank you.  Pick what you want from our stash."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Refurbishments Pt. V"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
msgid "Obtain a shovel."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
msgid ""
"Our sanitation here has become… problematic.  We've mostly just been going "
"outside the walls to piss.  Not only is it kinda unhealthy, but the last time "
"I wandered out I almost got eaten!  So, if you'd get us a shovel, we could "
"make a latrine for ourselves.  We'll pay you fairly, as usual."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
msgid "A hardware store should have one lying around."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
msgid "Do you have the shovel?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
msgid "Thank you.  We're eternally grateful to you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. V"
msgid "I'll do it myself, then."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Description of mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgid "Obtain a charcoal smoker."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgid ""
"Turns out that ant meat you got us wasn't actually too bad.  A little tough, "
"sure, but perfectly edible.  The problem now is we need a way of preserving "
"it.  One of those portable charcoal smokers would be really great.  Heck, you "
"might even wanna buy some."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgid ""
"Maybe try a farm?  I bet those rural folks were pretty invested in preserving "
"their food."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgid "Do you have the charcoal smoker?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/other/homeless/group_camp/group_camp_missions.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Refurbishments Pt. VI"
msgid "Thank you.  We'll get started right away."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/portal_storm/Portal_NPC.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ A person from elsewhere.
msgid "Involuntary Traveler"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/portal_storm/Portal_NPC.json
#. ~ Snippet in category "<end_talking_bye_portal_person>"
msgid "Pfum."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/portal_storm/Portal_NPC.json
#. ~ Job description of "No class" NPC class
msgid "I'm from another world."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/portal_storm/Portal_NPC.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Dell hastro bovice?  Arand natick res?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/portal_storm/Portal_NPC.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What?"
msgstr "Co?"

#: data/json/npcs/portal_storm/Portal_NPC.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Jand rawdle?  Ignate hasture."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/portal_storm/Portal_NPC.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I guess there's no reason to expect an interdimensional traveler to speak "
"English."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"My god, you've got to get me out of here.  The things… the things they've "
"done… please help."
msgstr ""
"Mój Boże, musisz mnie stąd zabrać. Te rzeczy… te rzeczy, które oni zrobili… "
"Proszę, pomóż."

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Aren't you a little short to be a stormtrooper?"
msgstr "Nie jesteś za niski, żeby być szturmowcem?"

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/talk_rescue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Please, help me."
msgstr "Proszę, pomóż mi."

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Can you get me out of this hell hole?"
msgstr "Możesz mnie wyciągnąć z tej piekielnej czeluści?"

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/talk_rescue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Who are you?  Are you real?"
msgstr "Kim jesteś? Jesteś prawdziwy?"

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/talk_rescue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Can you please save me?  I have to get out of here."
msgstr "Możesz mnie ocalić, proszę? Muszę się stąd wydostać."

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/talk_rescue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hallelujah, rescue!"
msgstr "Alleluja, ratunek!"

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/talk_rescue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I can't believe my eyes.  Thank you, thank you!"
msgstr "Nie wierzę własnym oczom. Dziękuję, dziękuję!"

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/npc/talk_rescue.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "You're… you're actually real!"
msgstr "Ty… faktycznie jesteś prawdziwy!"

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Come with me, if you want to live."
msgstr "Choć ze mną jeśli chcesz żyć."

#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've no use for weaklings.  Run.  Now."
msgstr "Nie mam pożytku ze słabeuszy. Biegnij. Już."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you have anything that you'd like to sell?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where did you say you were going again?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Have you found anything out of the ordinary out in the wastes?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"What's in that RV of yours?  Couldn't be anything you need, so hand over your "
"stuff."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Good to meet you too.  What are you doing out here?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&You describe the warehouse to the best of your ability.  <npc_name> "
"considers for a moment"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
", nodding along.  \"Yeah, I remember something like that a while back.  "
"Pretty memorable building, I think it's what you're looking for.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm going south.  Hopefully somebody down there fared better than the people "
"I knew up here.  Besides, I won't have to worry about freezing my <freaking> "
"butt off when winter comes."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm going west, see how things are out there in tumbleweed territory.  You "
"see, the Midwest didn't have a whole lot of people in it compared the East "
"Coast, so there logically shouldn't be as many <zombies> as there are here.  "
"I just hope that everything hasn't collapsed, that someone's still holding on."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "ERROR: DIRECTION PARAMETERS EITHER NOT PICKED OR OUT OF BOUNDS"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "When will you be leaving?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'll be gone here in a day or two, just stopping long enough to get some "
"supplies and fix anything wrong with the camper."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't have a whole lot, but I've got a few things that I could stand to be "
"rid of, too much weight tanks the gas mileage.  I could always use more fuel, "
"food, and clean water if you have any to spare.  Entertainment is also "
"appreciated, it's pretty fucking boring looking at nothing but road for 10 "
"hours a day."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's take a look."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How do I get to that farm?"
msgstr "Jak dostać się na tę farmę?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How do I get to that cabin?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where were they at?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Ah, that's nothing new to me.  Thanks anyway though."
msgstr "Ah, to nic nowego dla mnie. Ale i tak dzięki."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that farm"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that cabin"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that desolate barn"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that scrap metal castle"
msgid "Be careful.  Seems like a rough place to me."
msgstr "Bądź ostrożny. Wygląda mi to na niebezpieczne miejsce."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that farm"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that cabin"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that desolate barn"
msgid "Sweet."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that farm"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that cabin"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that desolate barn"
msgid "That's unfortunate."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Check out that desolate barn"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Random NPC, non persistent, tells you about being a guard and directs you
#. to free merchants.
#. ~ Random NPC, non persistent, doesn't have much to say.
msgid "Caravan Guard"
msgstr "Strażnik karawany"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/obsoletion_and_migration_0.I/obsolete_npc_class.json
#. ~ Job description of "Trader" NPC class
msgid "I'm collecting gear and selling it."
msgstr "Zbieram sprzęt i sprzedaję go."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We're just travelers, making a pit stop.  Might be willing to trade a bit, if "
"you've got anything to share.  We're not looking for trouble, there's plenty "
"of that on the roads already."
msgstr ""
"Jesteśmy wędrowcami robiącymi przystanek. Możemy być skłonni trochę "
"pohandlować, jeżeli masz coś, czym mógłbyś się podzielić. Nie szukamy "
"kłopotów, jest ich pełno na drodze."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We're with a larger group of survivors, working out of one of the old FEMA "
"bunkers.  Folks have taken to calling us Free Merchants, although that sounds "
"kinda on the nose to me.  We know about a few survivor groups and we make "
"regular trips around, sharing supplies back and forth and bringing them home. "
" We're on the way back now."
msgstr ""
"Jesteśmy z większą grupą ocalałych, działamy z jednego ze starych bunkrów "
"FEMA. Ludzie zaczęli nazywać nas Wolnymi Handlarzami, aczkolwiek brzmi to "
"dokładnie czym jesteśmy. Wiemy o kilku grupach ocalałych i regularnie ich "
"objeżdżamy, dzieląc się zasobami w tą i z powrotem oraz sprowadzając ich do "
"domu. Jesteśmy właśnie w drodze powrotnej."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where is 'home'?"
msgstr "Gdzie jest „dom”?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Here, I'll mark it on your map.  Feel free to come by and trade, or if you're "
"the type, we might have use for your services as a merc."
msgstr ""
"Tutaj, zaznaczę na twojej mapie. Czuj się swobodnie odwiedzić nas i "
"pohandlować lub jeśli wolisz, moglibyśmy skorzystać z twoich usług w "
"charakterze najemnika."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, thanks.  Well, let's trade."
msgstr "Jasne, dzięki. Cóż, pohandlujmy."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Always good to do a little trading."
msgstr "Zawsze dobrze trochę pohandlować."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Actually I had a little more to trade still."
msgstr "Tak właściwie, mam jeszcze trochę do handlowania."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sup?  Nice to see a survivor.  If you're here for business, talk to the "
"trader."
msgstr ""
"Co tam? Fajnie zobaczyć ocalałego. Jeśli masz jakiś interes, pogadaj z "
"handlarzem."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for the tip."
msgstr "Dzięki za poradę."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hi again.  You want something?"
msgstr "Witaj ponownie. Chcesz coś?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You looking for work?  I might be hiring."
msgstr "Szukasz pracy? Może ciebie zatrudnię."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nope, just saying hi."
msgstr "Nie, po prostu się witam."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm a caravan guard, working for the Free Merchants.  I'm an independent "
"contractor though.  Seems like a good way to get safety in numbers and try to "
"find a safe place to settle down."
msgstr ""
"Jestem strażnikiem karawany, pracującym dla Wolnych Handlarzy. Jestem jednak "
"niezależnym kontraktorem. Wydaje się to być dobry sposób na bycie bezpiecznym "
"w grupie, szukając bezpiecznego miejsca by się osiedlić."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So you're working for these guys, but aren't one of them?"
msgstr "Pracujesz zatem dla tych ludzi, ale nie jesteś jednym z nich?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"The Free Merchants?  Do they have some kind of trade outpost or anything like "
"that?"
msgstr "Wolni Handlarze? Mają oni jakąś placówkę handlową lub coś w tym stylu?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It's a living, eh?  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, these guys snagged some kind of FEMA evacuation bunker during the early "
"part of <the_cataclysm> and hoard the space.  They don't let anyone else "
"join, but they need supplies, so they send out traders, and those traders "
"need protection, so they send out guys like me."
msgstr ""
"Tak, ci ludzie przejęli jakiś bunkier ewakuacyjny FEMA podczas wcześniej "
"części <the_cataclysm> i opanowali miejsce. Nie pozwalają dołączyć byle komu, "
"ale potrzebują zapasów, więc wysyłają handlarzy, a ci handlarze potrzebują "
"ochrony, więc wysyłają takich ludzi jak ja."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How do I get there?"
msgstr "Jak mogę się tam dostać?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm good for the moment, but you can usually find a merc or two waiting "
"between jobs, back at the Free Merchant base."
msgstr ""
"Na razie jestem zadowolony, ale zazwyczaj można znaleźć najemnika lub dwóch "
"czekając pomiędzy robotami w bazie Wolnych Handlarzy."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for the tip!  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Dzięki za radę! <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Sure, I can mark it on your map if you like.  Here."
msgstr "Jasne, mogę zaznaczyć to na twojej mapie. Tutaj."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for the tip!  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "Dzięki za radę! <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*tips their hat down from their eyes and looks at you blearily.  \"Huh?  Hey, "
"I'm tryin'a sleep here.  I was on night watch."
msgstr ""
"*Odchyla kapelusz ze swoich oczu i patrzy na ciebie blado. „Co? Hej, próbuję "
"tutaj spać. Byłem na nocnej zmianie."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
#. ~ A survivor who sometimes visits the refugee center.
msgid "John Bailey"
msgstr "John Bailey"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*looks up at you, taking a moment to place your face, then grins broadly.  He "
"looks about the same as when you last saw him, perhaps a little more fit.  "
"\"So, you're still playing on the 'living' team, huh?  Glad to see you're "
"still kicking around.  Always good to run into a familiar face nowadays.\""
msgstr ""
"*Spogląda na ciebie, przez chwilę przyglądając się twojej twarzy, po czym "
"uśmiecha się szeroko. Wygląda mniej więcej tak samo, jak wtedy, gdy widziałeś "
"go po raz ostatni, może trochę bardziej sprawnie. „Więc nadal grasz w »żywej« "
"drużynie, co? Cieszę się, że wciąż się kręcisz. W dzisiejszych czasach zawsze "
"dobrze jest spotkać znajomą twarz”."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*glances your way, then makes eye contact as you move closer to speak.  He is "
"a strong-looking man in his mid forties, his hair graying and his face "
"flecked with stubble and travel dust.  The clothes he's wearing are clearly "
"scavenged, though they fit well, and he has the build of someone who until "
"recently had the luxury of carrying a few extra pounds.  \"Hi there.\"  He "
"presents his hand to shake.  \"You don't look like you belong here.  Name's "
"Bailey, John Bailey.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi John.  What are you doing here?"
msgstr "Cześć John. Co tu robisz?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hi John.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr "Cześć John. <end_talking_leave>"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*nods as you approach, then smiles and stretches casually.  \"Anything I can "
"do for you, friend?\""
msgstr ""
"*Kiwa głową, gdy podchodzisz, po czym uśmiecha się i rozciąga swobodnie. „Czy "
"mogę coś dla ciebie zrobić, przyjacielu?”."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What do you know about this place?"
msgstr "Co wiesz o tym miejscu?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You looking for any kind of work?"
msgstr "Szukasz jakiejś pracy?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm looking for a very specific building in the wilderness.  Have you seen it?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not at the moment, thanks."
msgstr "W tej chwili nie, dzięki."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Like I said,\" John shrugs.  \"I'm just checking "
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Same as you, I imagine,\" John shrugs.  \"Checking "
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"the place out, doing a little shopping.  Then I'll be on my way again.  Might "
"see if they have any work that needs done first, if the price is right."
msgstr ""
"to miejsce, robię małe zakupy. Potem znów ruszam w drogę. Może najpierw "
"zobaczę, czy nie potrzebują czegoś do zrobienia, jeśli cena będzie "
"odpowiednia."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What are you shopping for?"
msgstr "Co kupujesz?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "On your way\" where?"
msgstr "Po drodze” dokąd?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What kind of work are you looking for?"
msgstr "Jakiego rodzaju pracy szukasz?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Got time to teach me anything?"
msgstr "Masz czas, żeby mnie czegoś nauczyć?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sounds about the same as me, yep.  I'd better get back to it."
msgstr "Brzmi mniej więcej tak samo jak ja, tak. Lepiej do tego wrócę."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't really know.  Food stocks aren't too bad for me and mine, I found a "
"stock of canned goods early on that will last us for a while yet.  I don't "
"use a gun if I can avoid it, too noisy.  I notice these guys seem to keep a "
"lot of building supplies though, and trying to get a vehicle downtown to loot "
"a hardware store or a lumberyard is suicide, so I think that's where they're "
"going to get my money.  I wonder if they deliver."
msgstr ""
"Nie bardzo wiem. Zapasy żywności nie są takie złe, wcześnie znalazłem zapasy "
"konserw, które wystarczą nam jeszcze na jakiś czas. Nie używam broni, jeśli "
"mogę tego uniknąć, jest zbyt hałaśliwa. Zauważyłem, że ci ludzie trzymają "
"dużo artykułów budowlanych, a próba dojechania do centrum miasta, żeby "
"splądrować sklep z narzędziami lub tartak, to samobójstwo, więc myślę, że tak "
"zdobędą moje pieniądze. Ciekawe, czy dostarczą."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where are you headed next?"
msgstr "Dokąd zmierzasz w najbliższym czasie?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Who is \"you and yours\"?"
msgstr "Kto to jest „ty i twój”?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are you looking for work?"
msgstr "Szukasz pracy?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&You describe the warehouse to the best of your ability.  John listens "
"intently"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
", then shakes his head.  \"I don't believe I've heard about anything like "
"that, no.  Sorry.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
", looking thoughtful.  \"I can't guarantee it, but I'm pretty sure I've seen "
"something like that.  It was far away, and the weather was bad.  Could've "
"been a church or something, but it didn't look right for that.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh well, thanks John.  I'll go ask around."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You'd do better to talk to the people here about it.  Seems like a bunch of "
"them gathered here in the early days of <the_cataclysm> and managed to make "
"it through.  It's the biggest bunch of survivors I've found yet, but most of "
"them hunker up in the basement.  I can understand the urge.  We've all been "
"through way too much.  They say they don't have room for more people though, "
"so I'm just here to do some shopping, see if there's work to be done, then "
"move on."
msgstr ""
"Lepiej będzie, jeśli porozmawiasz o tym z tutejszymi ludźmi. Wygląda na to, "
"że kilku z nich zebrało się tutaj, jak na początku panował <the_cataclysm> i "
"udało im się przetrwać. Jest to największa grupa ocalałych, jaką udało mi się "
"znaleźć, ale większość z nich ukrywa się w piwnicy. Rozumiem tę potrzebę. "
"Wszyscy przeszliśmy już zbyt wiele. Mówią, że nie mają miejsca dla więcej "
"osób, więc jestem tu tylko po to, żeby zrobić zakupy, sprawdzić, czy jest "
"jakaś praca do wykonania, a potem ruszyć dalej."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "\"Move on\" where?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Who can say, really?  I don't really have a strong plan.  Depends on how this "
"trip goes.  Once my vehicle is full up, I'll have to head back to my hideout "
"and check on everyone there.  I don't like being gone too long."
msgstr ""
"Kto może powiedzieć w sumie? Tak naprawdę nie mam żadnego konkretnego planu. "
"To zależy od tego, jak potoczy się ta podróż. Kiedy mój pojazd będzie pełny, "
"będę musiał wrócić do mojej kryjówki i sprawdzić, co u wszystkich. Nie lubię "
"zbyt długo przebywać poza domem."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Who is \"everyone\"?"
msgstr "Kim są „wszyscy”?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Huh, well, the short story is, I got my wife and kids out of town in the "
"really, really early days.  She's got great intuition for stuff and when she "
"told me to get ready to leave town, I figured at worst we'd have an "
"unnecessary early spring vacation in my dad's old cabin, you know?  "
"Obviously, turns out trusting her gut saved us all and then some.  Things "
"were still tough, but from what I've heard, I might be the only person left "
"on the Eastern Seaboard who still has his whole nuclear family.  Still got a "
"lot of survivor's guilt for that… still lost everyone else.  Anyway, one "
"thing led to another and we gathered a few other people that we watch out "
"for.  My man Darius, he joined up early on and he and I do the scouting and "
"scavenging and watch each others' backs."
msgstr ""
"W skrócie chodzi o to, że wywiozłem żonę i dzieci z miasta w bardzo wczesnych "
"dniach. Ona ma świetną intuicję i kiedy powiedziała mi, żebym przygotował się "
"do wyjazdu z miasta, pomyślałem, że w najgorszym razie będziemy mieli "
"niepotrzebne wczesnowiosenne wakacje w starej chacie mojego ojca, wiesz? "
"Oczywiście okazało się, że zaufanie do jej przeczucia uratowało nas "
"wszystkich i jeszcze trochę. Nadal było ciężko, ale z tego, co słyszałem, "
"mogę być jedyną osobą na wschodnim wybrzeżu, która nadal ma całą swoją "
"rodzinę. Nadal mam poczucie winy za to, że przeżyłem… straciłem wszystkich "
"innych. Tak czy inaczej, jedna rzecz doprowadziła do drugiej i zebraliśmy "
"kilka innych osób, na które uważamy. Mój człowiek, Darius, dołączył do nas na "
"samym początku i razem z nim prowadzimy zwiad, szukamy i pilnujemy się "
"nawzajem."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Where are you guys located?  Can I join up too?"
msgstr "Gdzie się znajdujecie? Czy ja też mogę się przyłączyć?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Tell me about Darius."
msgstr "Opowiedz mi o Dariusie."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you know things were going to go wrong?"
msgstr "Skąd wiedziałeś, że wszystko pójdzie nie tak?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That seems like a pretty unlikely story."
msgstr "Wydaje się, że to dość nieprawdopodobna historia."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you give me any advice?"
msgstr "Czy możesz udzielić mi jakiejś rady?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What did you used to do before?"
msgstr "Czym zajmowałeś się wcześniej?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Let's change the subject.  What did you say you were doing here?"
msgstr "Zmieńmy temat. Co mówiłeś, że tu robisz?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'll be straight with you, I don't want to tell you too much about my people, "
"okay?  You seem all right, don't get me wrong, but I've seen some scary "
"fuckin' people out there, who come on all normal and then try to bite your "
"face off when they get you alone.  Everyone's reaction to the world's end is "
"a bit different.  Things are stable with my people now, but we don't really "
"welcome new faces anymore.  I wish it weren't that way.  Maybe if you and I "
"get to know each other better some day, I'll change my mind."
msgstr ""
"Będę z tobą szczery, nie chcę ci za dużo mówić o moich ludziach, dobrze? "
"Wydajesz się w porządku, nie zrozum mnie źle, ale widziałem tam strasznych, "
"pieprzonych ludzi, którzy zachowują się normalnie, a potem próbują odgryźć ci "
"twarz, kiedy zostaną z tobą sami. Każdy reaguje na koniec świata inaczej. W "
"moich stronach jest teraz stabilnie, ale nie witamy już nowych twarzy. "
"Chciałbym, żeby tak nie było. Może jeśli kiedyś poznamy się lepiej, zmienię "
"zdanie."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Your whole story seems a bit unlikely."
msgstr "Cała twoja historia wydaje się mało prawdopodobna."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Talk to Darius if you want to know about Darius.  He's a good man, and he "
"won't bite-- ugh, sorry, that's a turn of phrase we should probably retire, "
"hey?  Anyway.  I don't know if we'd have made it through the first days "
"without him.  He gets a bit jumpy around crowds since the riots though, so "
"he's out watching our stuff."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sometimes, I kinda wonder why other people *didn't* know things were going to "
"go wrong.  Hindsight is twenty-twenty, I guess.  I'll be honest though, as "
"much as I'd like to pat myself on the back, it wasn't me that figured it out. "
" When the really early riots started out, even though they were way up in the "
"Midwest, my wife just had a bad feeling.  We'd been thinking of a getaway "
"anyway, and I had some time off, so we took it as an excuse to get out to the "
"cabin and wait for everything to blow over.  Here we are.  It wasn't so much "
"knowing how things were going to go, more just straight luck that we trusted "
"our - *her* - gut at the right time and lucked out."
msgstr ""
"Czasami zastanawiam się, dlaczego inni ludzie nie wiedzieli, że coś pójdzie "
"nie tak. Patrząc wstecz, mam wrażenie, że to dopiero początek. Przyznam "
"szczerze, że choć bardzo chciałbym się pochwalić, to nie ja na to wpadłem. "
"Kiedy zaczęły się naprawdę wczesne zamieszki, mimo że miały miejsce na "
"środkowym zachodzie, moja żona miała złe przeczucia. I tak myśleliśmy o "
"ucieczce, a ja miałem trochę wolnego czasu, więc potraktowaliśmy to jako "
"pretekst, żeby wyjechać do domku i poczekać, aż wszystko ucichnie. I oto "
"jesteśmy. Nie tyle wiedzieliśmy, jak się sprawy potoczą, co po prostu "
"mieliśmy szczęście, że w odpowiednim momencie zaufaliśmy naszemu - jej - "
"przeczuciu i mieliśmy szczęście."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*chuckles.  \"Lucky for me then it doesn't matter if you believe me.  I do "
"gotta say though, it's funny you and I, a pair of actual real-live zombie "
"hunters, are talking face to face and you think my *survival story* is the "
"unlikely thing.\""
msgstr ""
"*Chichocze. „Na szczęście dla mnie nie ma znaczenia, czy mi wierzysz. Muszę "
"jednak przyznać, że to zabawne, że ty i ja, para prawdziwych łowców zombie, "
"rozmawiamy twarzą w twarz, a ty uważasz moją *opowieść o przetrwaniu* za coś "
"nieprawdopodobnego”."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I do odd jobs if people need help.  Not on a volunteer basis you understand, "
"but I try not to be unfair about it either.  Lots of people need a bit of "
"help these days, often just with little things a scavenger like me can find "
"for them.  It's easy for folks like you and me to underestimate how scared a "
"lot of people are to go back out in that place.  The situation's bad enough "
"as it is, but these kind of people took refuge back when it was true chaos "
"out there.  Lots of trauma to unpack there.  Anyway, if there's little things "
"I can do for them, I try to help where I can, so long as it doesn't put me in "
"too much danger."
msgstr ""
"Wykonuję dorywcze roboty, jeśli ludzie potrzebują pomocy. Nie jako "
"wolontariat, ale staram się też nie być nieuczciwy. W dzisiejszych czasach "
"wielu ludzi potrzebuje pomocy, często tylko w drobiazgach, które taki "
"zbieracz jak ja może dla nich znaleźć. Takim ludziom jak ja i ty łatwo jest "
"nie doceniać tego, jak wielu ludzi boi się wrócić w to miejsce. Sytuacja jest "
"już wystarczająco zła, ale tacy ludzie schronili się tam, kiedy panował tam "
"prawdziwy chaos. Mamy wiele traumatycznych przeżyć, z którymi trzeba się "
"uporać. W każdym razie, jeśli mogę zrobić dla nich jakąś drobną rzecz, staram "
"się pomóc, o ile nie naraża mnie to na zbyt duże niebezpieczeństwo."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"You look like you can handle yourself in a fight.  What's your zombie kill "
"count?"
msgstr "Wygląda na to, że radzisz sobie w walce. Jaką masz liczbę zabitych zombie?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I could use someone like you.  Want to travel with me?"
msgstr "Przydałby mi się ktoś taki jak ty. Chcesz ze mną podróżować?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You seem to know a lot about how people feel."
msgstr "Wygląda na to, że dużo wiesz o tym, co czują ludzie."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You've got that right.  People like you and I are made of stronger stuff."
msgstr "Masz rację. Ludzie tacy jak ty i ja są zrobieni z mocniejszych rzeczy."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"People should learn to fend for themselves, not just get you to hand "
"everything to them."
msgstr ""
"Ludzie powinni nauczyć się sami o siebie dbać, a nie tylko wymagać, abyś im "
"wszystko podawał."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*laughs a bit sheepishly.  \"Seems distasteful to keep track of that stuff, "
"doesn't it?\"  He touches a series of notches on his <mywp>.  \"I'm human "
"though.  I'm up to <npc_val:zkc_john> so far.  Seems like a lot to me, "
"especially since I try to avoid actually engaging the enemy if I can help it.\""
msgstr ""
"*Śmieje się trochę wstydliwie. „Wydaje się niesmaczne śledzenie tych rzeczy, "
"co?”. Dotyka serii nacięć na jego <mywp>. „Jestem jednak człowiekiem. Do tej "
"pory mam <npc_val:zkc_john>. Wydaje mi się, że to dużo, zwłaszcza, że staram "
"się unikać walki z wrogiem, jeśli mogę pomóc”."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*sizes you up and down, and shakes his head sadly.  \"Darius and I have a "
"good thing going, and a third person would be hard to justify, especially "
"these days.  Trust comes hard.  I'm sorry.  I hope you've got someone to "
"watch your back, but it can't be me.\""
msgstr ""
"*Przygląda się tobie i kręci smutno głową. „Darius i ja dobrze się "
"dogadujemy, a trudno byłoby uzasadnić obecność trzeciej osoby, zwłaszcza w "
"dzisiejszych czasach. Zaufanie przychodzi z trudem. Przykro mi. Mam nadzieję, "
"że masz kogoś, kto będzie cię pilnował, ale to nie mogę być ja”."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"That's a shame.  We'd be a good team.  People like you and I are made of "
"stronger stuff."
msgstr ""
"To wielka szkoda. Stanowilibyśmy dobry zespół. Ludzie tacy jak ty i ja są "
"zrobieni mocniejszych rzeczy."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Damn straight.  People should learn to fend for themselves."
msgstr "Tak jest. Ludzie powinni nauczyć się radzić sobie sami."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, I, uh… I know a bit about that stuff.  Hard not to empathize, "
"especially when I know I'm not quite as hard as others, by sheer luck.  "
"Besides, there are so few of us left now.  What's the point in wasting time "
"judging other people for how hard they took the end of the world?"
msgstr ""
"Tak, ja, eee… trochę o tym wiem. Trudno nie współczuć, zwłaszcza gdy wiem, że "
"nie jest mi tak ciężko jak innym, ze względu na zwykłe szczęście. Poza tym "
"zostało nas już tak niewielu. Jaki jest sens tracić czas na ocenianie innych "
"ludzi za to, jak ciężko znoszą koniec świata?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It sounds like you have some past there.  You want to talk about it?"
msgstr "Wygląda na to, że masz za sobą jakąś przeszłość. Chcesz o tym porozmawiać?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Not really, no.  It's old stuff, and there's enough going on.  Let's just say "
"I'm no stranger to loss, either my own or others'."
msgstr ""
"Nie do końca. To stare sprawy i wystarczająco dużo się dzieje. Powiedzmy, że "
"nie jest mi obca strata, zarówno moja własna, jak i innych."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*raises an eyebrow.  \"I don't know about that.  You should be careful about "
"thinking people who don't make the same choices as you are inferior.  Sure, "
"not everyone's suited to scavenge, but a scavenger's got to have a safe home, "
"too.\""
msgstr ""
"*Unosi brew. „No nie wiem. Powinieneś uważać, żeby nie myśleć, że ludzie, "
"którzy nie dokonują takich samych wyborów jak ty, są gorsi. Jasne, nie każdy "
"nadaje się do zbieractwa, ale zbieracz też musi mieć bezpieczny dom”."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Fuck that.  People should learn to fend for themselves."
msgstr "Pieprzyć to. Ludzie powinni nauczyć się radzić sobie sami."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*rubs his stubble, looking thoughtful.  \"I agree it's important to be "
"independent, but don't forget, working together is what makes us better than "
"the undead.  It's how we got out of the trees and fields, and into "
"civilization.  Anyway, I don't want to talk philosophy at you.  If you're "
"doing well on your own, more power to you!\""
msgstr ""
"*Drapie się po zaroście, patrząc w zamyśleniu. „Zgadzam się, że niezależność "
"jest ważna, ale nie zapominaj, że to właśnie współpraca czyni nas lepszymi od "
"nieumarłych. To dzięki niej wydostaliśmy się z drzew i łąk do cywilizacji. W "
"każdym razie nie chcę mówić do ciebie filozofii. Jeśli dobrze sobie radzisz "
"sam, to bardzo dobrze!”."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That's for the weaklings.  People like you and I are made of stronger stuff."
msgstr ""
"To jest dla słabeuszy. Ludzie tacy jak ty i ja są zrobieni z mocniejszych "
"rzeczy."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't know, the zombies sure seem to work together to me."
msgstr "Nie wiem, dla mnie zombie wydają się współpracować."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"*chuckles.  \"If you can call it that, sure.  So maybe we should do our best "
"to be better at that than the zombies.  Seems pretty reasonable to me, and "
"it's a pretty low bar to clear.\""
msgstr ""
"*Chichocze. „Jeśli można to tak nazwać, to pewnie. Więc może powinniśmy "
"zrobić wszystko, żeby być w tym lepsi od zombie. Wydaje mi się to całkiem "
"rozsądne, a poprzeczka do pokonania jest całkiem niska”."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure, I guess.  I don't know if I know anything you don't, you seem like you "
"can handle yourself.  I've made it this far by not engaging whenever "
"possible.  I'm never going to kill all the zombies out there.  Darius and I "
"try not to fight if we can avoid it, and if we can't, we try to always have "
"the advantage.  Numbers, weaponry, terrain.  Zombies are clumsy and stupid so "
"we lead them across bushes and things to trip and stumble.  We take high "
"ground and let them plough into ladders like idiots while we stick 'em with "
"spears from above.  Mostly, though, we try not to be seen.  We use bikes "
"instead of cars because they don't make noise and don't need gas, plus we can "
"take forest trails and things and avoid traffic jams.  Those things are "
"suicide.  We try to avoid the cities, and when we do go close, we stick to "
"the outskirts and raid the outlying houses.  In those, we keep crouched and "
"try to get deep into the building fast, or down into the basement, so that "
"little noises don't carry much and nothing from outside can see us.  Also, "
"zombies being idiots, closing the blinds is a great move.  I always keep a "
"crowbar for opening doors and windows, but I try not to use it if I can avoid "
"it.  Darius can pick locks, which is slower but doesn't make noise.  We get a "
"lot more mileage from raiding gas stations and other rural sites, where if "
"there are a few zombies, we can usually lead them away."
msgstr ""
"Pewnie, że tak. Nie wiem, czy wiem coś, czego ty nie wiesz, wyglądasz, jakbyś "
"umiał sobie poradzić. Dotarłem tak daleko dzięki temu, że nie angażowałem "
"się, kiedy tylko było to możliwe. Nigdy nie uda mi się zabić wszystkich "
"zombie. Darius i ja staramy się nie walczyć, jeśli możemy tego uniknąć, a "
"jeśli nie możemy, staramy się zawsze mieć przewagę. Liczebność, uzbrojenie, "
"ukształtowanie terenu. Zombie są niezdarne i głupie, więc prowadzimy je przez "
"krzaki i inne rzeczy, aby się potykały. Zajmujemy wysoki teren i pozwalamy im "
"wlec się po drabinach jak idiotom, podczas gdy my wbijamy im włócznie z góry. "
"Przede wszystkim jednak staramy się, żeby nas nie było widać. Używamy rowerów "
"zamiast samochodów, bo nie hałasują i nie potrzebują benzyny, a poza tym "
"możemy jeździć leśnymi ścieżkami i unikać korków. Takie rzeczy to "
"samobójstwo. Staramy się unikać miast, a jeśli już się do nich zbliżamy, to "
"trzymamy się obrzeży i napadamy na domy na obrzeżach. W takich domach kucamy "
"i staramy się szybko dostać w głąb budynku lub do piwnicy, tak aby drobne "
"dźwięki nie przenosiły się zbytnio i aby nikt z zewnątrz nas nie widział. "
"Ponadto zombie to idioci, więc zasłanianie żaluzji jest świetnym posunięciem. "
"Zawsze mam przy sobie łom do otwierania drzwi i okien, ale staram się go nie "
"używać, jeśli mogę tego uniknąć. Darius potrafi otwierać zamki, co jest "
"wolniejsze, ale nie robi hałasu. Dużo więcej korzyści przynosi nam napadanie "
"na stacje benzynowe i inne wiejskie miejsca, gdzie jeśli jest kilka zombie, "
"zwykle możemy je odciągnąć."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What about things other than zombies?"
msgstr "A co z rzeczami innymi niż zombie?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, jeez, yeah.  The world really went to shit, didn't it?  Well, I've seen "
"some weird alien things.  Our rule is 'scared is better than dead'.  If we "
"don't know what something is and how to kill it, we steer wide and clear.  "
"One time I saw this flaming eyeball a long way off, I was scouting from a "
"cell phone tower.  It made eye contact with me and I just started "
"hallucinating shit.  Darius stopped me from falling right off the tower.  "
"Stuff like that is why I think you have to be a bit off your rocker to travel "
"these days unless you have no choice.  Anything we don't know, we turn around "
"and pedal hard.  So far, we haven't met anything our bikes can't outrun."
msgstr ""
"O Jezu, tak. Świat naprawdę się pojebał, co? Cóż, widziałem kilka dziwnych "
"obcych rzeczy. Nasza zasada brzmi: „lepiej się bać niż być martwym”. Jeśli "
"nie wiemy, co to jest i jak to zabić, trzymamy się od tego z daleka. Pewnego "
"razu zobaczyłem płomienną gałkę oczną z daleka, kiedy prowadziłem zwiad z "
"wieży telefonii komórkowej. Nawiązała ze mną kontakt wzrokowy, a ja zacząłem "
"mieć halucynacje. Darius powstrzymał mnie przed upadkiem z wieży. Takie "
"rzeczy sprawiają, że uważam, że w dzisiejszych czasach trzeba być trochę "
"stukniętym, żeby podróżować, chyba że nie ma się wyboru. Jeśli czegoś nie "
"wiemy, zawracamy i ostro pedałujemy. Jak dotąd nie spotkaliśmy niczego, czego "
"nasze rowery nie byłyby w stanie prześcignąć."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's a tougher question than you might think.  I've had quite the life.  My "
"dad was a mechanic, and when I was young I used to help around the shop quite "
"a bit.  I started out thinking I was going to get into that line of work, but "
"then I got sidetracked and wound up getting into computers and electrical "
"work for a long time.  Did part of an electrical engineering degree, then "
"decided it wasn't for me and quit that.  Spent a bit of time doing freelance "
"electrical and programming work, then got recruited by a startup that was "
"designing and programming medical equipment.  I was supposed to be a general "
"technician, but through a weird series of events I wound up in sales, then "
"management.  I hated management, and I'd made a big nest egg from my share "
"stock, so I cashed out and tried to retire young.  That was a dumb move, I "
"was bored as hell, so I finished off my degree and started doing on-call "
"teaching work for shop, computers, math, and things like that at a college "
"and high school level.  Just part time, and I spent the rest of my time "
"outdoors, hiking and whatnot."
msgstr ""
"To pytanie jest trudniejsze, niż mogłoby się wydawać. Miałem całkiem ciekawe "
"życie. Mój tata był mechanikiem, a kiedy byłem mały, często pomagałem w "
"warsztacie. Na początku myślałem, że będę pracował w tym zawodzie, ale potem "
"zepchnięto mnie na boczny tor i przez długi czas zajmowałem się komputerami i "
"elektryką. Ukończyłem część studiów na kierunku elektrotechnika, po czym "
"zdecydowałem, że to nie dla mnie i zrezygnowałem. Trochę czasu spędziłem, "
"pracując jako wolny strzelec w branży elektrycznej i programistycznej, a "
"potem zostałem zatrudniony przez firmę zajmującą się projektowaniem i "
"programowaniem sprzętu medycznego. Miałem być ogólnym technikiem, ale w "
"wyniku dziwnego splotu wydarzeń trafiłem do działu sprzedaży, a potem do "
"zarządu. Nienawidziłem zarządzania, a na akcjach zarobiłem sporą sumę, więc "
"spieniężyłem ją i próbowałem przejść na młodą emeryturę. To było głupie "
"posunięcie, nudziłem się jak cholera, więc skończyłem studia i zacząłem "
"pracować jako korepetytor techniki, komputerów, matematyki i tym podobnych "
"przedmiotów na poziomie szkoły średniej i wyższej. Tylko w niepełnym wymiarze "
"godzin, a resztę czasu spędzałem na świeżym powietrzu, wędrując i nie tylko."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "That is one hell of a life.  You must have some useful skills to teach."
msgstr ""
"To jest dopiero życie. Musisz mieć jakieś przydatne umiejętności, których "
"możesz nauczyć."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'd be happy to.  I can't spare a lot of free time, but for a little trade, "
"I'll tell you about whatever I can help with."
msgstr ""
"Chętnie. Nie mam zbyt wiele wolnego czasu, ale za niewielką opłatą opowiem ci "
"o wszystkim, w czym będę mógł pomóc."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sorry, but that's all I have time for at the moment.  Darius is waiting "
"outside."
msgstr ""
"Przepraszam, ale to wszystko, na co mam w tej chwili czas. Darius czeka na "
"zewnątrz."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure, let's talk trade."
msgstr "Jasne, wymieńmy się."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll bear that in mind.  What did you say you were doing here?"
msgstr "Będę o tym pamiętał. Co mówiłeś, że tu robisz?"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks, I'll think about it.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I might take you up on that, but for now I've gotta go."
msgstr "Może się na to zgodzę, ale na razie muszę lecieć."

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Random NPC, can direct you to the free merchants and nearest FEMA camp.
#. ~ Random NPC, can be recruited away.
#. ~ Random NPC, demands heroin and can accept.
msgid "refugee"
msgstr "Uchodźca"

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Please don't hurt us, we're just trying to get to safety."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's your situation here?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I don't mean any harm.  I'm looking for a specific, strange building.  I "
"wonder if you've heard anything about it?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't have time for zombie bait like you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No, I don't have any."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We're just trying to find a safe place right now.  I think there's a FEMA "
"camp nearby that should have room for us."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Good luck with that.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"&You describe the warehouse to the best of your ability.  The refugee nods "
"along"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ", then frowns.  \"Nope, not ringing any bells, sorry.\""
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"We were at the same little evacuation hut, but it was all messed up, just "
"used condoms and broken bottles and lipstick writing on the walls.  We found "
"another group of refugees like us on the road, but they had all been killed, "
"all ripped up, blood everywhere.  We took their food and made it all the way "
"to a big refugee center, but somebody there with a gun told us there was no "
"room, so we're going to a FEMA camp.  They should have more room and "
"supplies.  No guarantees, but it's a chance."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Can you give me directions to that FEMA camp?  I want to go there too if it's "
"so great."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I haven't been to any refugee center.  Can you tell me where it is?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Of course, we're all in this together.  Let me mark that on your map."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thanks for the information.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
msgid "Things must be better at the camp…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
msgid "We're all in this together, looking forward to meeting you there."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
msgid "Everything is going to be all right."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
msgid "No worries friend, good luck to you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
msgid "The hard part is getting there."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
msgid "Any progress on getting to the camp?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
msgid "Well, success I guess."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
msgid "Such a disappointment…"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Here, I'll mark it on your map.  I wouldn't bet they'll treat you any "
"differently than us though.  You might try and bring something to trade, they "
"like that."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can you give me directions to where you're going too?  I love cartography."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Looking good there.  I like your whole setup.  What's your story?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Nice.  Good to see you again.  What do you want from me?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Affirmative response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You should come with me instead."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Negative response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You should definitely come with me instead."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nothing, just saying hi."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So you're not attached right now?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why, where were you before?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Not interested.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No, I'm not really with them.  We just got stuck together in the same messed "
"up evacuation place.  This one guy was really nice, but they wouldn't let us "
"stay.  They got there first so they told us we needed to find our own place, "
"but if we got anything they wanted they'd trade some of the stuff they have.  "
"I tried to talk them into helping but they were so cold to me."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yeah, I guess it's hard all over.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "This is the beginning of a beautiful thing.  I'm with you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/liam_chat.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yes!"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Actually, I think I'm on the right track here, but you might have some luck "
"finding a little something something back at the Free Merchant base.  They "
"seemed pretty desperate."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Of course.  How do I get there?"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Yes.  I'll be on my way then."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey man.  Do you have any heroin?  I'm in a bit of a bind."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Never, that heroin is for me and me alone."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I think you might need it even more than me.  Here you go."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I love you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Oh, uh, thanks.  I guess."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No thank you."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/missiondef_free_merchants.json
#: data/mods/classic_zombies/missiondef.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Reach Refugee Center"
msgstr "Idź do centrum uchodźców"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Description of effect type "Full"
msgid "This beggar in the refugee center has had something to eat recently."
msgstr "Ten żebrak w centrum uchodźców niedawno coś zjadł."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
#. ~ Hungry beggar in the refugee center.
msgid "Reena Sandhu"
msgstr "Reena Sandhu"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a female NPC
#. ~ Hungry beggar in the refugee center.
msgid "Teacher"
msgstr "Nauczycielka"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ All the beggars have been camping inside the evac shelter because they're
#. too weak and unskilled to make it on their own.
#. ~ This is the only beggar with some skills, sort of the leader.
msgid "Beggar"
msgstr "Żebrak"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "So, any luck with convincing the others to come on your crazy adventure yet?"
msgstr ""
"To co, udało ci się przekonać pozostałych do wzięcia udziału w twojej "
"szalonej wyprawie?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Thank you again.  I really appreciate the food."
msgstr "Dziękuję ci raz jeszcze. Jestem bardzo wdzięczny za posiłek."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Please, help me.  I need food.  Aren't you their sheriff?  Can't you help me?"
msgstr ""
"Proszę, pomóż mi. Potrzebuję pożywienia. Nie jesteś aby ich szeryfem? Nie "
"możesz mi pomóc?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Please, help me.  I need food."
msgstr "Proszę pomóż mi, potrzebuję żywności."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I've talked to the others, and they're all willing to come.  So, you joining "
"us?"
msgstr "Rozmawiałem z pozostałymi i wszyscy są skłonni iść. Więc, dołączysz do nas?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Hey, here, I might have some food for you.  Let me check."
msgstr "Hej, tutaj, chyba mam jakąś żywność dla ciebie. Niech no sprawdzę."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Get away from me."
msgstr "Odejdź ode mnie."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"They won't let me in.  They say they're too full.  I'm allowed to camp out "
"here as long as I keep it clean and don't make a fuss"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ", but I'm reduced to begging to survive."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ", but I'm so hungry."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why don't you scavenge your own food?"
msgstr "Czemu nie zdobędziesz sam sobie jedzenia?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I might have some food for you.  Let me check."
msgstr "Mogę mieć jakąś żywność dla ciebie. Niech no sprawdzę."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I've got some more food, if you want it."
msgstr "Mam jeszcze trochę jedzenia, jeśli je chcesz."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry, I can't help you."
msgstr "Wybacz, nie mogę ci pomóc."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Thank you so much."
msgstr "Tak bardzo ci dziękuję."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Can I ask you something else first?"
msgstr "Mogę wpierw cię o coś innego zapytać?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'm sorry, I was wrong.  I can't help you."
msgstr "Wybacz, myliłem się, nie mogę ci pomóc."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Here, you can have this <topic_item>."
msgstr "Trzymaj, możesz wziąć <topic_item>."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "This is wonderful of you, I really appreciate it."
msgstr "To wspaniałe z twojej strony, naprawdę to doceniam."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No problem.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Where else?  I can't fight those things out there.  I'm in terrible physical "
"condition, don't have any useful skills, and I'm terrified of <zombies> and "
"violence.  How am I supposed to find a safe place?"
msgstr ""
"Niby gdzie? Nie mogę walczyć z tym na zewnątrz. Jestem w kiepskim stanie "
"fizycznym, nie mam użytecznych umiejętności, i przerażają mnie <zombies> i "
"przemoc. Jak mam znaleźć bezpieczne miejsce?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Come with me.  Maybe you're not the greatest adventurer, but it's better than "
"living here."
msgstr ""
"Chodź ze mną. Może nie jesteś najlepszym poszukiwaczem przygód, ale to lepsze "
"niż mieszkanie tutaj."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I have a camp of my own, away from here.  You could come there.  There aren't "
"many people left, we could use anyone regardless of skills."
msgstr ""
"Mam swój własny obóz, daleko stąd. Mógłbyś tam się udać. Nie zostało zbyt "
"wielu ludzi, przydałby się każdy, niezależnie od umiejętności."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Out there?  That's suicide!  People that go out there don't come back, people "
"who can hold their own… unlike me.  I'd rather take my chances begging for "
"scraps and waiting for someone in the center to die and make room for me, "
"thanks."
msgstr ""
"Tam? to samobójstwo! Ludzie którzy idą na zewnątrz nie wracają, tacy co wiążą "
"koniec z końcem… w przeciwieństwie do mnie. Dzięki, ale lepiej mi błagać o "
"resztki i czekać aż ktoś w środku umrze i zwolni mi miejsce."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I have a camp of my own, away from here.  Maybe you can't scavenge, but we "
"can use any warm bodies that can lift a tool.  You'd be safer and better fed "
"there."
msgstr ""
"Mam swój własny obóz, daleko stąd. Może nie możesz zająć się zbieractwem, ale "
"przyda nam się każdy żywy człowiek, który potrafi podnieść narzędzie. "
"Będziesz tam bezpieczniejszy i lepiej odżywiony."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I was a high school math teacher.  It was a good job, I loved it.  Funny "
"enough, it's not super applicable after the end of the world.  I mean, at "
"some point people are going to need a teacher again, but right now they just "
"want food, shelter, and clothing."
msgstr ""
"Byłem nauczycielem matematyki w szkole. To była dobra praca, kochałem ją. "
"Zabawne, ale nie jest zbyt pomocna po końcu świata. Wiem że w końcu ludziom "
"będą potrzebni nauczyciele, ale na razie potrzebują pożywienia, schronienia, "
"i ubrań."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I have a camp of my own, away from here.  Maybe they can't use your skills "
"here, but I could."
msgstr ""
"Mam swój własny obóz, daleko stąd. Może oni nie mogą wykorzystać twoich "
"umiejętności tutaj, ale ja mogę."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's a kind offer of you, but I think I'd rather take my chances here than "
"risking it out there again.  I remember <the_cataclysm>, I'm not in any hurry "
"to face that again."
msgstr ""
"To miła oferta z twojej strony, ale myślę, że wolę zaryzykować tutaj, niż "
"ryzykować tam ponownie. Pamiętam <the_cataclysm> i nie spieszy mi się, by "
"znów się z tym zmierzyć."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's quite the offer, but I don't think I'd survive the trip.  I don't "
"think you realize how useless I am in this world."
msgstr ""
"To niezła oferta, ale nie sądzę, żebym przeżył podróż. Chyba nie zdajesz "
"sobie sprawy, jak bardzo jestem bezużyteczny w tym świecie."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "I'm sorry, I'm too hungry to make a big decision like that."
msgstr "Wybacz, jestem zbyt głodny by podjąć tak ważną decyzję."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I can keep you safe.  I'll take you there myself."
msgstr "Mogę zapewnić ci bezpieczeństwo. Sam cię tam zabiorę."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I really appreciate everything you've done for me, but I don't think you get "
"it.  I can't go out there.  I will die.  I know it's horrible camping out "
"here, but I just can't face that nightmare again."
msgstr ""
"Naprawdę doceniam wszystko, co dla mnie zrobiłeś, ale nie sądzę, żebyś to "
"rozumiał. Nie mogę tam iść. Umrę. Wiem, że biwakowanie tutaj jest okropne, "
"ale nie mogę znów zmierzyć się z tym koszmarem."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I hope you'll reconsider eventually.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "OK.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "OK. <done_conversation_section>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "OK, I'll talk to them too."
msgstr "Ok. Z nimi też porozmawiam."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "All right!  <lets_go>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Schizophrenic beggar in the refugee center.
msgid "Dino Dave"
msgstr "Dinozaur Dave"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "We've done it!  We've solved the list!"
msgstr "Udało się! Wypełniliśmy tę listę!"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "How's things with you?  My cardboard collection is getting quite impressive."
msgstr "Jak tam u ciebie? Moja kolekcja kartonów robi się całkiem imponująca."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Have I told you about cardboard, friend?  Do you have any?"
msgstr "Czy mówiłem ci już o kartonie przyjacielu? Czy masz może jakiś?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "About that shopping list of yours…"
msgstr "A propos tej twojej listy zakupów…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Is there anything else I can do for you?"
msgstr "Jest coś jeszcze co mogę dla ciebie zrobić?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What are you going to do with all that cardboard now?"
msgstr "Co teraz zrobisz z tym całym kartonem?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"We've done it, Dave!  Smokes says you can build yourself a house up on the "
"roof if you want.  You've got to keep it nice and clean, and help out the "
"people down here by looking out for zombies, but you can still use the "
"washrooms and things downstairs when you need to.  What do you say?"
msgstr ""
"Udało nam się, Dave! Smokes mówi, że możesz zbudować sobie dom na dachu, "
"jeśli chcesz. Musisz utrzymywać go w czystości i pomagać ludziom na dole, "
"wypatrując zombie, ale w razie potrzeby możesz korzystać z łazienek i innych "
"rzeczy na dole. Co ty na to?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Cardboard?"
msgstr "Karton?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why are you sitting out here?"
msgstr "Czemu tu przesiadujesz?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Are you seriously wearing a dinosaur costume?"
msgstr "Na serio nosisz ten kostium dinozaura?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you need something to eat?"
msgstr "Potrzebujesz czegoś do jedzenia?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Oh nice.  Crunchings and munchings.  That's a cool, a cool thing."
msgstr "O miło. Chrupanie i mlaskanie. To fajna, fajna rzecz."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I can tell when it has stuff in it, it's got a sandy texture.  But this "
"doesn't.  Thanks again."
msgstr ""
"Mogę rozpoznać, kiedy ma w sobie coś ekstra, ma wtedy taką piaszczystą "
"konsystencję. Ale ta jest inna. Jeszcze raz dzięki."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "No problem.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I'm building a house out of cardboard.  The sandman doesn't want me to, but I "
"told him to go fuck himself."
msgstr ""
"Buduję dom z kartonu. Piaskowy dziadek nie chce, żebym to robił ale niech się "
"odpieprzy."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why cardboard?"
msgstr "Czemu karton?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "The sandman?"
msgstr "Piaskowy dziadek?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Would you like me to give you some cardboard?"
msgstr "Chciałbyś ode mnie dostać trochę kartonu?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"There's so much of it now, and the zombies are afraid of it.  It's kept me "
"safe so far.  The beta rays come from the center point of the zombie, so it "
"hits the cardboard and can't penetrate.  The reflection can stop any further "
"damage."
msgstr ""
"Tyle tego jest teraz, a zombie się go boją. Zapewnił mi bezpieczeństwo jak "
"dotąd. Promienie beta promieniują z centrum zombie, więc uderzają w karton i "
"nie mogą go przebić. Odbicie może zapobiec dalszym obrażeniom."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Kind of a question's that?  Yeah man, you got cardboard, I got a whole… a "
"whole shopping list.  Got it here."
msgstr ""
"Co to za pytanie? Tak, ty masz tekturę, ja mam całą… całą listę zakupów. Mam "
"ją tutaj."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's next on the list?"
msgstr "Co jest następne na liście?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If you don't know who he is, I definitely can't tell you.  He talks to "
"everyone, if you didn't hear him that means you can't be trusted, except to "
"help me out."
msgstr ""
"Jeśli nie wiesz, kim on jest, to na pewno nie mogę ci powiedzieć. Rozmawia z "
"każdym, jeśli go nie słyszałeś, to znaczy, że nie można ci ufać, chyba że po "
"to, by mi pomóc."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "…<done_conversation_section>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"These cowards are afraid of me.  They won't let me into their base.  I'm "
"going to build my new house and I won't let them in."
msgstr ""
"Ci tchórze boją się mnie. Nie wpuszczą mnie do swojej bazy. Zbuduję sobie "
"nowy dom i ich też nie wpuszczę."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You said you were building a house?"
msgstr "Wspominałeś, że budujesz dom?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I… I can see you wearing it.  Why are you wearing that?"
msgstr "Widzę…, że masz to na sobie. Dlaczego to nosisz?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What was that about cardboard?"
msgstr "O co chodziło z tym kartonem?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/mods/DinoMod/NPC/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You ask me what I can see, but I don't tell you what you see.  Sometimes we "
"have shields up, to protect ourselves."
msgstr ""
"Pytasz mnie, co widzę, ale ja nie mówię ci, co ty widzisz. Czasami mamy "
"podniesione tarcze, żeby się chronić."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Well… I had it all pretty together, "
msgstr "No cóż… miałem to wszystko ładnie poukładane, "

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "but the others have left, and "
msgstr "ale inni odeszli, a "

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "and I feel bad with all the help you've given me already, but "
msgstr "i czuję się źle, biorąc pod uwagę całą pomoc, jakiej mi już udzieliłeś, ale  "

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"now the masters won't let me build my sanctuary.  I know I can't build it in "
"here, they wouldn't allow it.  They won't listen to me when I ask for a safe "
"place.  They just want me to disappear, like the others.  Can you help me "
"figure them out?"
msgstr ""
"teraz mistrzowie nie pozwalają mi zbudować mojego sanktuarium. Wiem, że nie "
"mogę go zbudować tutaj, nie pozwoliliby na to. Nie słuchają mnie, kiedy "
"proszę o bezpieczne miejsce. Chcą, żebym po prostu zniknął, tak jak inni. Czy "
"pomożesz mi ich rozgryźć?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Why don't you leave this place?  Come with me, I could use some help out "
"there."
msgstr ""
"Dlaczego nie opuścisz tego miejsca? Chodź ze mną, przydałaby mi się jakaś "
"pomoc."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Sure, Dave.  One last favor, I think I can talk to Smokes about finding you a "
"place to go."
msgstr ""
"Jasne, Dave. Jeszcze jedno, myślę, że mogę porozmawiać z Smokesem o "
"znalezieniu dla ciebie miejsca."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have to think on that, Dave, I've done a lot already."
msgstr "Muszę się nad tym zastanowić, Dave, wiele już zrobiłem."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"The roof!  So high!  So lofty!  I can hardly believe it!  This will be a "
"nicer house than I had before everything went funny.  I can watch out, I'm "
"happy to do that.  And it'll be nice to still have a bathroom!  Come see me "
"there, my friend.  I will not disappoint you."
msgstr ""
"Dach! Tak wysoki! Taki wzniosły! Aż trudno w to uwierzyć! To będzie "
"ładniejszy dom niż ten, który miałem, zanim wszystko się popsuło. Mogę się "
"pilnować, jestem szczęśliwy, że mogę to zrobić. I miło będzie mieć jeszcze "
"łazienkę! Przyjdź do mnie, mój przyjacielu. Nie zawiodę cię."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll see you on the rooftop.  Good luck, Dave."
msgstr "Do zobaczenia na dachu. Powodzenia, Dave."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No!  I just got everything together.  I am not leaving, not now.  "
"Everything's finally coming together!"
msgstr ""
"Nie! Dopiero co wszystko pozbierałem do kupy. Nie odejdę, nie teraz. W końcu "
"wszystko zaczyna się układać!"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Well, OK then, Dave.  One last favor, I think I can talk to Smokes about "
"finding you a place to go."
msgstr ""
"No to dobrze, Dave. Jeszcze jedno, myślę, że mogę porozmawiać z Smokesem o "
"znalezieniu dla ciebie miejsca."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I'll have to think on it, Dave, I've done a lot already."
msgstr "Będę musiał się nad tym zastanowić, Dave, wiele już zrobiłem."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
msgstr "Przynieś 40 małych kartonowych pudeł"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
msgid ""
"Gotta start small right?  Little ones for keeping little things safe.  I "
"could use 'em."
msgstr ""
"Trzeba zacząć od małych, co nie? Małe do bezpiecznego przechowywania małych "
"rzeczy. Przydałyby mi się."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
msgid ""
"Gotta start small right?  Little ones for keeping little things safe.  I "
"could use 'em.  I need a bunch of 'em.  Little ones, you know?  Can you bring "
"me like… like… forty?"
msgstr ""
"Trzeba zacząć od małych, prawda? Małe do ochrony małych rzeczy. Przydadzą mi "
"się. Potrzebuję ich kilka. Małych, wiesz? Możesz mi przynieść jakieś… jakieś… "
"czterdzieści?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
msgid "Oh man, thanks so much my friend.  You won't regret it."
msgstr "O rany, wielkie dzięki przyjacielu. Nie będziesz żałował."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
msgid "I didn't think so."
msgstr "Nie sądzę…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
msgid "Watch out, he's looking for it too."
msgstr "Uważaj, on też ich szuka."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
msgid "Got the little ones yet?"
msgstr "Masz już te małe?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
msgid "Oh this is so great, so great!"
msgstr "O to świetnie, wspaniale!"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 40 small cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
msgid "Oh, that's too bad.  Guess they're eating it all."
msgstr "Och, to niedobrze. Pewnie pozjadali wszystko."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
msgstr "Przynieś rolkę taśmy klejącej (200 ładunków)."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
msgid ""
"These ones are good, good ones.  They need something to, you know, bind them "
"together.  Surround them, light side, dark side."
msgstr ""
"Te są dobre, dobre. Potrzebują czegoś, co, no wiesz, co połączy je razem. "
"Owinąć je, jasna strona, ciemna strona."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
msgid ""
"These ones are good, good ones.  They need something to, you know, bind them "
"together.  Surround them, light side, dark side.  Bring me the Force!"
msgstr ""
"Te są dobre, dobre. Potrzebują czegoś, co, no wiesz, co połączy je razem. "
"Owinąć je, jasna strona, ciemna strona. Daj mi Moc!"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring a roll of duct tape (200 charges)"
msgid "It's all around us… but did you get it in a crude matter form?"
msgstr "Jest wszędzie wokół nas… ale czy zdobyłeś ją w formie surowej materii?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
msgid "Ten bigger ones now please.  The list doesn't lie.  You've done so well."
msgstr "Teraz dziesięć większych poproszę. Lista nie kłamie. Tak dobrze ci poszło."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
msgid ""
"Ten bigger ones now please.  The list doesn't lie.  You've done so well.  I "
"got a little more on the list, but we're more than half there."
msgstr ""
"Teraz dziesięć większych poproszę. Lista nie kłamie. Tak dobrze ci poszło. "
"Mam trochę więcej punktów na liście, ale to już ponad połowa."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
msgid "Any luck?  Bigger ones?"
msgstr "Poszczęściło się? Te większe?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 cardboard boxes"
msgid "I'm so happy now!"
msgstr "Jestem taki szczęśliwy!"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
msgstr "Przynieś 10 dużych plastikowych płacht"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
msgid ""
"If I can set it up in here I won't need it, but they might drive me out, so I "
"guess I need some plastic just in case.  I don't like it, the sandman can "
"smell through plastic, but I think the cardboard is stronger."
msgstr ""
"Jeśli uda mi się go ustawić tutaj, nie będzie mi on potrzebny, ale mogą mnie "
"wygonić, więc chyba potrzebuję trochę plastiku na wszelki wypadek. Nie podoba "
"mi się to, piaskowy dziadek potrafi wyczuć zapach przez plastik, ale karton "
"chyba jest silniejszy."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
msgid ""
"If I can set it up in here I won't need it, but they might drive me out, so I "
"guess I need some plastic just in case.  I don't like it, the sandman can "
"smell through plastic, but I think the cardboard is stronger.  Please bring "
"me some plastic sheets."
msgstr ""
"Jeśli uda mi się go ustawić tutaj, nie będzie mi on potrzebny, ale mogą mnie "
"wygonić, więc chyba potrzebuję trochę plastiku na wszelki wypadek. Nie podoba "
"mi się to, piaskowy dziadek może czuć zapach przez plastik, ale myślę, że "
"karton jest silniejszy. Proszę, przynieś mi trochę plastikowych arkuszy."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
msgid "We're almost there, now."
msgstr "Już prawie jesteśmy gotowi."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
msgid "They keep a lot of this stuff in hardware stores and lumber yards."
msgstr "Trzymają wiele z tych rzeczy w sklepach z narzędziami i tartakach."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
msgid ""
"I really feel bad sending you on this one, it's dangerous.  Have you found "
"anything?"
msgstr ""
"Naprawdę czuję się źle wysyłając cię po to, to jest niebezpieczne. Znalazłaś "
"coś?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
msgid "Nice, this will do perfectly!"
msgstr "Nieźle, to się nada doskonale!"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 10 large plastic sheets"
msgid "Oh, that's too bad."
msgstr "O, to niedobrze."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
msgstr "Przynieś 5 dużych kartonowych pudeł"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
msgid ""
"This is the last thing I need from you.  I've been collecting the other parts "
"myself, it's been easier with more cardboard around.  Can you bring me five "
"more really big cardboard boxes?"
msgstr ""
"To ostatnia rzecz, jakiej od ciebie potrzebuję. Sam zbierałem pozostałe "
"części, było to łatwiejsze z większą ilością kartonu. Możesz mi przynieść "
"jeszcze pięć naprawdę dużych kartonowych pudeł?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
msgid ""
"This is the last thing I need from you.  I've been collecting the other parts "
"myself, it's been easier with more cardboard around.  Can you bring me five "
"more really big cardboard boxes?  Five more cardboard boxes, as big as it "
"gets.  I have a few already stored up, that should be all I need."
msgstr ""
"To ostatnia rzecz, jakiej od ciebie potrzebuję. Sam zbierałem pozostałe "
"części, było to łatwiejsze z większą ilością kartonu. Możesz mi przynieść "
"jeszcze pięć naprawdę dużych kartonowych pudeł? Pięć pudeł kartonowych, tak "
"dużych jak to tylko możliwe. Mam już kilka w zapasie, to powinno wystarczyć."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
msgid "Yes!  The home stretch!"
msgstr "Tak! Już prawie koniec!"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
msgid "Oh man, but we're so close!"
msgstr "O rety, a byliśmy tak blisko!"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
msgid "Try looking in cargo storage areas."
msgstr "Spróbuj poszukać w magazynach towarowych."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
msgid "Did you bring me those last few boxes?"
msgstr "Przyniosłeś mi tych kilka ostatnich pudeł?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
msgid ""
"Brilliant!  You're a true hero.  I'll see if I can find a place to set these "
"up now."
msgstr ""
"Genialnie! Jesteś prawdziwym bohaterem. Zobaczę, czy znajdę miejsce, żeby je "
"ustawić."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring 5 large cardboard boxes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
msgid "No!  Oh god, no, this can't be happening…"
msgstr "Nie! O Boże, nie, to nie może się dziać…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Mission name
msgid "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to call home."
msgstr ""
"Porozmawiaj z Smokesem o znalezieniu dla Dave’a miejsca, w którym mógłby "
"zamieszkać."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
msgid ""
"I have it, I have it all, but I can't find a place to put it.  Will you ask "
"the masters?  Maybe?  I've tried but they ignore me."
msgstr ""
"Mam to, mam to wszystko, ale nie mogę znaleźć miejsca, w którym mógłbym to "
"umieścić. Czy zapytasz mistrzów? Może? Próbowałem, ale oni mnie ignorują."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
msgid ""
"I have it, I have it all, but I can't find a place to put it.  Will you ask "
"the masters?  Maybe?  I've tried but they ignore me.  I just need a place to "
"put it all, a place I can be safe, and not make anyone upset."
msgstr ""
"Mam to, mam to wszystko, ale nie mogę znaleźć miejsca, w którym mógłbym to "
"umieścić. Czy zapytasz mistrzów? Może? Próbowałem, ale oni mnie ignorują. "
"Potrzebuję tylko miejsca, w którym mógłbym to wszystko umieścić, miejsca, w "
"którym byłbym bezpieczny i nie sprawiał nikomu przykrości."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
msgid "Thank you!  I'm sorry, I thought we were done, but we can do this!"
msgstr "Dziękuję! Przepraszam, myślałem, że to już koniec, ale damy radę!"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
msgid "Maybe somewhere they can't see me?  Where I can just be me?"
msgstr "Może gdzieś, gdzie nie mogą mnie zobaczyć? Gdzie będę mógł być sobą?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
msgid "Did you ask the masters?"
msgstr "Spytałeś mistrzów?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
msgid ""
"The roof!  So high!  So lofty!  Come see me there, my friend.  I will not "
"disappoint you."
msgstr ""
"Dach! Tak wysoki! Taki przestrzenny! Przyjdź tam do mnie, mój przyjacielu. "
"Nie zawiodę cię."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/npc/missiondef.json
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Talk to Smokes about finding Dave a place to
#. call home."
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Power Storage CBM"
msgid "I don't understand."
msgstr "Nie rozumiem."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Name of effect type id "insulted_luo"
msgid "Insulted"
msgstr "Obraza"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Description of effect type "Insulted"
msgid "Oh, you went there."
msgstr "Och, a więc to tak!"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
#. ~ Angry beggar in the refugee center.
msgid "Luo Meizhen"
msgstr "Luo Meizhen"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a female NPC
#. ~ Angry beggar in the refugee center.
msgid "Mycologist"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Yo.  Anyone else keen on moving from this bus stop to your tent city?"
msgstr ""
"Joł. Czy ktoś jeszcze chce się przenieść z tego przystanku do swojego "
"miasteczka namiotowego?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey there.  Good to see you again."
msgstr "Hej tam. Dobrze znów cię widzieć."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Careful, I'm getting hangry again and am not totally responsible for my own "
"actions."
msgstr ""
"Ostrożnie, znowu robię się głodny i nie biorę pełnej odpowiedzialności za "
"swoje czyny."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Don't bother with these assholes."
msgstr "Nie przejmuje się tymi dupkami."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I might have some food for you.  Are you hungry?"
msgstr "Mogę mieć jakąś żywność dla ciebie. Głodny?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "We're cool.  Sorry for insulting you earlier."
msgstr "Spoko. Wybacz że cię zelżyłem wcześniej."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I found a sample of alien fungus for you."
msgstr "Znalazłem dla ciebie próbkę obcego grzyba."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Ok… see ya."
msgstr "Okej… do zobaczenia."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Actually yeah, I'm always hungry these days.  I don't like taking handouts, "
"but I wouldn't say no."
msgstr ""
"Właściwie to tak, ostatnio zawsze jestem głodny. Nie lubię brać jałmużny, ale "
"nie odmówiłbym."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Thanks, I really appreciate this."
msgstr "Dziękuję, naprawdę to odceniam."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "They're 'too full'.  Won't share fuck-all."
msgstr "Są „zbyt zapchani”. Niczym się nie podzielą."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why are you living here then?"
msgstr "Czemu zatem tu mieszkasz?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Well, they might not share, but I can.  Are you hungry?"
msgstr "Cóż, może oni się nie podzielą, ale ja mogę. Jesteś głodny?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Even without them helping, it's the safest place to squat.  As long as we "
"keep it clean up here and don't cause sanitation problems, they don't mind us "
"sitting around the entryway.  So kind and generous of them, to let us sit "
"here and slowly starve."
msgstr ""
"Nawet bez ich pomocy, to najbezpieczniejsze miejsce by przycupnąć. Dopóki "
"dbamy o czystość i nie sprawiamy problemów sanitarnych, nie mają nic "
"przeciwko byśmy siedzieli obok wejścia. To miło z ich strony że pozwalają nam "
"tu siedzieć i umierać z głodu."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh, same old story at first.  I got evacuated on to the local concentration "
"center, then picked up on a repurposed school bus and dragged out here.  Then "
"the chick processing me to get in saw my face and Chinese name and "
"conveniently 'lost' my paperwork.  I was sent out here to wait for further "
"processing, while I watched busloads of people get processed and taken in.  "
"By the time they 'found' it, the place was full up, wouldn't ya know it.  Now "
"I'm stuck out here and they won't consider letting me in."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/your_followers/luo_follower.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You think you were treated like that because of your race?"
msgstr "Myślisz, że byłeś tak traktowany z powodu swojej rasy?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Does that mean you were part of that back room evacuation I heard about?"
msgstr "Czy to oznacza, że byłeś częścią ewakuacji z zaplecza, o której słyszałem?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why stay out here then?"
msgstr "Czemu tu zatem zostałeś?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I have a camp of my own, away from here.  No paperwork required.  Want to "
"come?"
msgstr ""
"Mam swój własny obóz, daleko stąd. Bez zbędnej papierologii. Chcesz do nas "
"dołączyć?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh yeah, that was a hell of a shitstorm.  We were waiting back there for "
"'processing' for hours and hours, with the sick and wounded.  One guy died, "
"we all thought he was sleeping until he got back up.  That started a panic, "
"gunshots in a closed area, that kind of stuff.  In just a few minutes, a "
"bunch more people were dead.  Then the assholes called it an 'outbreak' and "
"tried to barricade us in… took us way too long to convince the panicking "
"guards that we were alive and needed to get out.  I'll give the one guy "
"credit, Sean: when he found out they'd locked living people in with zombies, "
"he came in himself, as some of the newly dead were starting to get back up, "
"and he held them off for us to escape.  That… that was probably the only "
"actual good thing I've seen since before the end of the world: he owned his "
"error and he put himself in harm's way to make up for it.  Massive respect to "
"that guy.  So, of course, he's a zombie now.  Fuck, thanks for reminding me "
"of all that sunny fun."
msgstr ""
"O tak, to była niezła rozpierducha. Godzinami czekaliśmy tam na „załatwianie” "
"wraz z chorymi i rannymi. Jeden facet zmarł, wszyscy myśleliśmy, że spał, "
"dopóki nie powrócił. Zaczęła się panika, strzały w zamkniętym obiekcie, tego "
"typu rzeczy. W ciągu kilku minut zginęło o wiele więcej ludzi. Wtedy te dupki "
"nazwały to „epidemią” i próbowały nas zabarykadować… Zajęło nam zbyt dużo "
"czasu, by przekonać spanikowanych strażników, że żyjemy i musimy się "
"wydostać. Oddam sprawiedliwość jednemu facetowi, Seanowi: kiedy dowiedział "
"się, że zamknęli żywych ludzi z zombie, sam wszedł do środka, kiedy niektórzy "
"z niedawno zmarłych zaczęli się podnosić i powstrzymał ich, abyśmy mogli "
"uciec. To… to była chyba jedyna dobra rzecz, jaką widziałem od czasów przed "
"końcem świata: uznał swój błąd i naraził się na niebezpieczeństwo, by go "
"naprawić. Ogromny szacunek dla tego faceta. Więc, oczywiście, jest teraz "
"zombie. Kurwa, dzięki za przypomnienie mi o całej tej wspaniałej zabawie."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sorry for bringing it up. What were you saying?"
msgstr "Wybacz, że to wywlekam. O czym to mówiłeś?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Sure.  My grandparents were from China.  That means I'm obviously personally "
"responsible for all this.  Do you think there's some other reason they let "
"hundreds of other educated people in and I'm sitting out here?"
msgstr ""
"Jasne. Moi dziadkowie pochodzili z Chin. To znaczy, że jestem za to wszystko "
"osobiście odpowiedzialny. Myślisz, że jest jakiś inny powód, dla którego "
"wpuścili setki innych wykształconych ludzi, a ja tu siedzę?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I don't care if you're Chinese.  You can travel with me if you want."
msgstr ""
"Nie obchodzi mnie czy jesteś chińczykiem. Możesz podróżować ze mną, jeśli "
"chcesz."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I mean, racism could definitely be a part of it… but you are visibly in poor "
"shape.  They need strong survivor material."
msgstr ""
"To znaczy, rasizm może być częścią tego, ale ty jesteś w kiepskiej formie. "
"Potrzebują silnego materiału na ocalałych."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's awful kind of you, but look at me.  I'm not traveling material, I've "
"managed to stay fifty pounds overweight on a diet of pine nuts and wilted "
"rhubarb, and I scream and shake uncontrollably at the sight of blood."
msgstr ""
"To strasznie miłe z twojej strony, ale spójrz na mnie. Nie jestem materiałem "
"na podróżnika, udało mi się utrzymać pięćdziesiąt funtów nadwagi na diecie "
"złożonej z orzeszków piniowych i zwiędłego rabarbaru, a na widok krwi krzyczę "
"i trzęsę się bez opamiętania."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"It'd be temporary.  I have a base set up.  There are only a few of us "
"survivors left, we need to work together"
msgstr ""
"Tylko tymczasowo. Mam założoną bazę. Zostało nas niewielu ocalałych, musimy "
"pracować razem."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Okay, yeah, that's a bit of a problem.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It may not be much, but we've got a little community.  We can't live like "
"this forever, but we're safer than out there, and we look out for each other. "
" One way or another we'll shake things out to something better."
msgstr ""
"Może to nie jest dużo, ale mamy małą społeczność. Nie możemy tak żyć "
"wiecznie, ale jesteśmy bezpieczniejsi niż tam, i dbamy o siebie nawzajem. W "
"ten czy inny sposób doprowadzimy sprawy do jakiegoś lepszego porządku."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You sound more optimistic than usual."
msgstr "Brzmisz bardziej optymistycznie niż zazwyczaj."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "So, about that doctorate of yours…"
msgstr "A więc, jeśli chodzi o twój doktorat…"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Don't get me wrong, I hate this place and this situation, and especially the "
"selfish racist fucks that landed me here… but these other losers that landed "
"out here with me?  I like them.  We might be miserable, but we're miserable "
"together."
msgstr ""
"Nie zrozum mnie źle, nienawidzę tego miejsca i całej tej sytuacji, a "
"zwłaszcza tych samolubnych rasistowskich skurwieli, którzy mnie tu wpakowali… "
"ale ci inni frajerzy, którzy wylądowali tu ze mną? Lubię ich. Może i jesteśmy "
"żałośni, ale jesteśmy żałośni razem."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Thanks for saying it.  So, what brings you around?"
msgstr "Dzięki, że to powiedziałeś. Więc, co cię tu sprowadza?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Just wanted to get square.  <end_talking_leave>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Tempting offer, but I don't know how much I trust a random stranger offering "
"me a place to live.  Call me crazy."
msgstr ""
"Kusząca oferta, ale nie wiem, na ile ufam przypadkowemu nieznajomemu, który "
"oferuje mi mieszkanie. Nazwij mnie szalonym."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Oh, come on.  I'm not a random stranger anymore, I brought you that crazy "
"mushroom didn't I?"
msgstr ""
"No, dajże spokój. Nie jestem już jakimś przypadkowym nieznajomym, przyniosłem "
"ci przecież tego zwariowanego grzybka, prawda?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"What better choice do you have?  It's not like it would be just you and me, "
"the others out here can come too."
msgstr ""
"Jaki masz lepszy wybór? To nie jest tak, że będziemy tylko ty i ja, pozostali "
"obecni tutaj też mogą przyjść."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Like I said, sorry, it's just not happening.  It's not that I don't trust "
"you, it's just that I don't really trust you."
msgstr ""
"Jak mówiłem, przykro mi, ale tak się nie stanie. Nie chodzi o to, że ci nie "
"ufam, tylko o to, że nie ufam ci naprawdę."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Aw damn, I was worried you'd say that.  Okay, listen: you've got yourself a "
"deal.  I'll come to your base, but you've gotta get me hooked up with a "
"microscope as soon as you can.  This could be the beginning of something "
"really cool.  Oh, and it should go without saying that I'm not coming unless "
"you can find a place for my friends here in your base.  I'm sure you "
"anticipated that.  Talk them into going and I'm in.  It should be easy, "
"they're a bunch of sweet hearted saps."
msgstr ""
"Cholera, bałem się, że to powiesz. Dobra, słuchaj: mamy umowę. Pójdę do "
"twojej bazy, ale musisz mi załatwić mikroskop, tak szybko jak tylko będziesz "
"mógł. To może być początek czegoś naprawdę fajnego. Aha, i nie trzeba mówić, "
"że nie przyjdę, jeśli nie znajdziesz miejsca dla moich przyjaciół w swojej "
"bazie. Jestem pewien, że to przewidziałeś. Namów ich na wyjazd i wchodzę w "
"to. To powinno być łatwe, to banda słodkich, serdecznych mięczaków."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, before <the_cataclysm> ended I was working at a university bookstore.  "
"I know a little bit about a lot of things, I guess you could say.  I kinda "
"loved the job, to be honest."
msgstr ""
"Cóż, przed końcem <the_cataclysm> pracowałem w uniwersyteckiej księgarni. "
"Wiem trochę o wielu rzeczach, myślę, że można tak powiedzieć. Szczerze "
"mówiąc, kochałem tę pracę."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"What had you working at the university bookstore in the first place?  Are you "
"an academic yourself?"
msgstr "Nad czym pracowałeś w uniwersyteckiej księgarni? Czy sam jesteś akademikiem?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's this I hear about you having a doctorate?"
msgstr "Słyszałem coś o tym, że masz doktorat?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, yeah, it's all very glamorous.  Sure, I trained in the great ivory "
"tower, got my PhD in mycology.  Did my dissertation on signaling pathways in "
"hyphae formation, and a postdoc in plant-fungus communication in rhizomes.  "
"Then I got the job at the bookstore because there wasn't a ton of work for a "
"doctor of mycology, although I'd had a few nibbles before things really got "
"crazy.  Now, people are just breaking down my door to get my sweet sweet "
"knowledge of mold to help them fight the incoming zombie threat."
msgstr ""
"Tak, tak, wszystko jest bardzo efektowne. Jasne, trenowałem w wielkiej wieży "
"z kości słoniowej, uzyskałem doktorat z mikologii. Zrobiłem moją rozprawę na "
"temat szlaków sygnałowych w tworzeniu strzępek i postdok w komunikacji "
"roślin-grzybów w kłączach. Potem dostałem pracę w księgarni, ponieważ nie "
"było wiele pracy dla lekarza mikologii, przynajmniej miałem kilka przekąsek, "
"zanim wszystko naprawdę oszalało. Teraz ludzie po prostu wyłamują moje drzwi, "
"aby uzyskać moją słodką słodką wiedzę na temat pleśni, aby pomóc im walczyć z "
"nadchodzącym zagrożeniem zombie."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you know about the fungal zombies though?"
msgstr "Wiesz o grzybowych zombie, prawda?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Heh.  Yeah, that was a great use of my time.  As you can see it really helped "
"my employment prospects.  Yeah, I have a PhD in mycology.  Did my "
"dissertation on signaling pathways in hyphae formation, and a postdoc in "
"plant-fungus communication in rhizomes.  Then I got the job at the bookstore "
"because there wasn't a ton of work for a doctor of mycology, although I'd had "
"a few nibbles before things really got crazy.  Now, people are just breaking "
"down my door to get my sweet sweet knowledge of mold to help them fight the "
"incoming zombie threat."
msgstr ""
"Heh. Tak, to było świetne wykorzystanie mojego czasu. Jak widać, naprawdę "
"pomogło to moim perspektywom zatrudnienia. Tak, mam doktorat z mikologii. "
"Zrobiłem moją rozprawę na temat szlaków sygnałowych w tworzeniu strzępek i "
"postdoc w komunikacji roślin-grzybów w kłączach. Potem dostałem pracę w "
"księgarni, ponieważ nie było mnóstwo pracy dla lekarza mikologii, "
"przynajmniej miałem kilka przekąsek, zanim wszystko naprawdę oszalało. Teraz "
"ludzie po prostu wyłamują moje drzwi, aby uzyskać moją słodką słodką wiedzę "
"na temat pleśni, aby pomóc im walczyć z nadchodzącym zagrożeniem zombie."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"No, no I don't, and I'd appreciate you not leaving me hanging on that.  There "
"are fungal zombies?"
msgstr ""
"Nie, nie, nie wiem i byłbym wdzięczny gdybyś nie kazał mi czekać na "
"odpowiedź. Tam są grzybowe zombie?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Encroaching alien mushrooms, fungal towers, tough mycelium invading ground "
"and trees, zombies taken over by aggressive mold… Yeah.  It's ugly stuff."
msgstr ""
"Zbliżają się obce grzyby, wieże grzybowe, twarda grzybnia atakująca ziemię i "
"drzewa, zombie opanowane przez agresywną pleśń… Tak. To brzydkie rzeczy."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Okay, you've got my attention.  Listen, do you think you could bring me some "
"kind of sample of these things?"
msgstr ""
"Dobra, przykułeś moją uwagę. Słuchaj, myślisz, że mógłbyś przynieść mi jakąś "
"próbkę tych rzeczy?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"It'd be dangerous.  What kind of benefit is there from taking a risk like "
"that?"
msgstr "To byłoby niebezpieczne. Jakie korzyści płyną z podjęcia takiego ryzyka?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"If you get me a sample, I'll join your crazy camp expedition.  Hell, if you "
"bring me a sample maybe I'll help you set up a lab to study this stuff.  "
"Almost anything could work, but if this stuff is as dangerous as you make it "
"sound, maybe make sure it's not a sporulating body."
msgstr ""
"Jeśli zdobędziesz dla mnie próbkę, dołączę do twojej szalonej obozowej "
"ekspedycji. Do diabła, jeśli przyniesiesz mi próbkę, może pomogę ci założyć "
"laboratorium do zbadania tego czegoś. Prawie wszystko może się nadać, ale "
"jeśli to coś jest tak niebezpieczne, jak mówisz, to może upewnij się, że to "
"nie jest ciało zarodnikujące."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I dunno, scientific interest?  If you don't bring me anything, no worries.  "
"I'm positively swimming in entertainment here, as you can see."
msgstr ""
"Nie wiem, zainteresowanie naukowe? Jeśli nic mi nie przyniesiesz, nie martw "
"się. Jak widzisz, pławię się tu w rozrywce."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "It just so happens I have a chunk of fungal matter on me right now."
msgstr "Tak się składa, że mam teraz przy sobie kawałek grzybów."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Sure, I'd better get going.  I'll see if I can find you something."
msgstr "Jasne, lepiej się już zbieram. Zobaczę czy mogę coś dla ciebie znaleźć."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well.  Well, well, well.  This is really interesting.  Look, you can see "
"reticulations here, it looks sort of like an enlarged piece of a stipe from a "
"basidiocarp… but look at this, these fibers are clearly unlike anything I've "
"seen before.  I wonder if they're motile?\n"
"\n"
"Okay, listen: you've got yourself a deal.  I'll come to your base, but you've "
"gotta get me hooked up with a microscope as soon as you can.  This could be "
"the beginning of something really cool.  Oh, and it should go without saying "
"that I'm not coming unless you can find a place for my friends here in your "
"base.  I'm sure you anticipated that.  Talk them into going and I'm in.  It "
"should be easy, they're a bunch of sweet hearted saps."
msgstr ""
"Dobrze. No, no, no. To jest naprawdę interesujące. Spójrz, widać tu "
"retikulacje, wygląda to jak powiększony kawałek łodygi z bazidiokarpu… ale "
"spójrz na to, te włókna są wyraźnie niepodobne do niczego, co widziałem "
"wcześniej. Ciekawe, czy są ruchliwe?\n"
"\n"
"Dobra, słuchaj: masz umowę. Przyjadę do twojej bazy, ale musisz mnie jak "
"najszybciej wyposażyć w mikroskop. To może być początek czegoś naprawdę "
"fajnego. Aha, i nie trzeba mówić, że nie przyjdę, jeśli nie znajdziesz "
"miejsca dla moich przyjaciół. Jestem pewien, że to przewidziałeś. Namów ich "
"na wyjazd i wchodzę w to. To powinno być łatwe, to banda słodkich, "
"serdecznych mięczaków."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Great!  I'll go see what I can do about that."
msgstr "Wspaniale! Pójdę zobaczyć co mogę z tym zrobić."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well.  Well, well, well.  This is really interesting.  Look, you can see "
"reticulations here, it looks sort of like an enlarged piece of a stipe from a "
"basidiocarp… but look at this, these fibers are clearly unlike anything I've "
"seen before.  I wonder if they're motile?\n"
"\n"
"Sorry.  I could stare at this all day.  I owe you one, a big one.  Thanks for "
"this.  Let me know if you ever need a favor from a chubby beggar woman."
msgstr ""
"Dobrze. No, no, no. To jest naprawdę interesujące. Spójrz, widać tu "
"retikulacje, wygląda to jak powiększony kawałek łodygi z bazidiokarpu… ale "
"spójrz na to, te włókna są wyraźnie niepodobne do niczego, co widziałem "
"wcześniej. Ciekawe, czy są ruchliwe?\n"
"\n"
"Przepraszam. Mogłabym się na to gapić cały dzień. Jestem ci winna przysługę, "
"i to dużą. Dzięki za to. Daj mi znać, jeśli kiedykolwiek będziesz potrzebował "
"przysługi od pulchnej żebraczki."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Glad you like it.  If I think of something you can do in return, I'll let you "
"know."
msgstr ""
"Cieszę się, że ci się podoba. Jeśli przyjdzie mi do głowy coś, co możesz "
"zrobić w zamian, dam Ci znać."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Well good.  Let's get going, I want to see some more of these crazy mushrooms."
msgstr ""
"No dobra. Zbierajmy się zatem, chcę zobaczyć jeszcze kilka tych obłędnych "
"grzybów."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Sickly beggar in the refugee center.
msgid "Brandon Garder"
msgstr "Brandon Garder"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_carpenter1.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_carpenter2.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
#. ~ Sickly beggar in the refugee center.
#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Flavor
#. ~ Construction skill trainer
msgid "Carpenter"
msgstr "Cieśla"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Hey, are you a big fan of survival of the fittest?"
msgstr "Hej, jesteś wielkim fanem przeżycia najlepszych?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why do you ask?"
msgstr "Czemu pytasz?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to see you too, what's up?"
msgstr "Mi też miło mi cię widzieć, co tam?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to see you.  I gotta be going though."
msgstr "Miło było się widzieć. Niestety, muszę już lecieć."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Oh you know, the usual: sittin' out here until I starve to death, playin' "
"cards with Dave, that kinda thing."
msgstr ""
"No wiesz, to co zwykle: siedzenie tutaj, aż umrę z głodu, granie w karty z "
"Davem, tego typu rzeczy."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Because I sure ain't fit, so I'm sittin' out here until I starve to death.  "
"Help a poor sickly soul out?"
msgstr ""
"Bo ja, to pewne, do najlepszych nie należę, więc posiedzę tu aż umrę z głodu. "
"Pomożesz biednej duszy w potrzebie?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I could maybe help you out… want something to eat?"
msgstr "Może mogę ci jakoś pomóc… chcesz coś do jedzenia?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What's wrong with you?"
msgstr "Co z tobą nie tak?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "They won't let you in because you're sick?"
msgstr "Nie wpuszczą cię bo jesteś chory?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "How did you even get here if you're so sick?"
msgstr "Jak się tu w ogóle dostałeś jak jesteś taki chory?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why are you camped out here if they won't let you in?"
msgstr "Czemu tu obozujesz skoro cię nie wpuszczą?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "That's awful kind of you, you really are a wonderful person."
msgstr "To strasznie miłe z Twojej strony, naprawdę jesteś wspaniałą osobą."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "It's good to know there are still people like you in the world, it really is."
msgstr "Dobrze wiedzieć, że na świecie są jeszcze tacy ludzie jak ty, naprawdę."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What are you up to?"
msgstr "Co tam porabiasz?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You name it!  Asthma, diabetes, arthritis.  Diabetes hasn't been so bad since "
"I stopped, y'know, eating regularly.  Well, I assume it hasn't.  Not like I "
"can check that ol' whatchamacallit, the blood test the docs used to bug me "
"about every couple months."
msgstr ""
"Do wyboru do koloru! Astma, cukrzyca, reumatyzm. Cukrzyca nie daje się we "
"znaki od kiedy, wiesz, przestałem jeść regularnie. Przynajmniej zakładam, że "
"nie ujawnia się. Nie żebym mógł zrobić, jak mu tam było, ten test krwi o "
"który lekarze upominali się raz na kilka miesięcy."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You seem awfully happy considering the situation."
msgstr "Czujesz niezmierne zadowolenie zważając na sytuację."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"They got enough mouths to feed that can pull their own weight.  I got a lot "
"of weight and I'm too weak to pull it, so I'm out here."
msgstr ""
"Mają wystarczająco gąb do wyżywienia które potrafią udźwignąć swoją wagę. Ja "
"mam za dużo wagi i jestem zbyt słaby, by ją udźwignąć, więc jestem tutaj."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Came with a small group quite a while ago.  The others were young and fit, "
"they got in.  They were some of the last ones to get in actually.  I didn't "
"make the cutoff."
msgstr ""
"Przybyłem z małą grupą jakiś czas temu. Tamci byli młodzi i sprawni, więc są "
"w środku. I tak byli jedynymi z ostatnich, którzy się dostali. Ja nie "
"spełniłem warunków."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"This is a mercy.  I get shelter, light, and heat, and those guards will help "
"us if any zombies show up.  It ain't so bad.  If I was out on my own I'd have "
"none of this and still have to look for food… in other words, I'd be dead as "
"a doornail.  Or I guess undead."
msgstr ""
"To jest litość. Mam schronienie, światło, ciepło, a strażnicy pomogą ja się "
"pojawi tu jakiś zombie. Nie jest tak źle. Gdybym był tam sam, nie maiłbym nic "
"z tych rzeczy a i tak musiałbym poszukiwać żarcia. Więc byłbym sztywny jak "
"grobowa deska. Albo w zasadzie nieumarły."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"What's the alternative?  You take the hand you're dealt.  I've given eulogies "
"for two of the people I love most on this earth, and the third wrote me off.  "
"I've already been through the end of the world.  Came out the other side with "
"my bits intact.  And you know, I've been pretty lonely since my wife passed.  "
"Here I've got friends.  We might be hungry but we're close.  Reena's been "
"teaching me math and science, Luo is one of the smartest folks I've ever met "
"- she's got a doctorate you know - and Yusuke is the only one here that can "
"beat me at poker.  And Dave, well, he's Dave.  There's more goin' on under "
"the surface there, mark my words.  We may be unfit, but we aren't worthless."
msgstr ""
"A jaka jest alternatywa? Bierzesz karty, które ci rozdano. Wygłosiłem mowę "
"pogrzebową dla dwóch osób, które najbardziej kocham na tej ziemi, a trzecia "
"spisała mnie na straty. Przeszedłem już przez koniec świata. Wyszedłem po "
"drugiej stronie ze wszystkimi kawałkami w całości. I wiesz, byłem dość "
"samotny, odkąd odeszła moja żona. Tutaj mam przyjaciół. Może jesteśmy głodni, "
"ale jesteśmy blisko. Reena uczy mnie matematyki i nauk ścisłych, Luo to jedna "
"z najmądrzejszych osób, jakie kiedykolwiek spotkałem - ma doktorat, wiesz - a "
"Yusuke jest jedynym człowiekiem tutaj, który może mnie pokonać w pokera. A "
"Dave, cóż, to Dave. Tam pod powierzchnią dzieje się więcej niż się zdaje, "
"zapamiętaj moje słowa. Możemy być niezdolni, ale nie jesteśmy bezwartościowi."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Well, I used to be a roofer, but I had a bad fall and wrecked my back around "
"'06.  Tried to get into other kinds of carpentry but I just don't have the "
"head for it.  My wife managed to support both of us with the extra bit I made "
"from odd jobs, but she had a stroke in 2016 and left me on my own the last "
"few years slowly draining my savings dry while I work whatever junk jobs I "
"can handle.  Couple days before <the_cataclysm> I got the notice that the "
"bank was going to foreclose on my crappy little trailer."
msgstr ""
"Cóż, kiedyś byłem dekarzem, ale zaliczyłem poważny upadek i rozwaliłem sobie "
"kręgosłup w okolicach szóstego kręgu. Próbowałem zająć się innymi rodzajami "
"ciesielstwa, ale po prostu nie mam do tego głowy. Moja żona zdołała utrzymać "
"nas oboje z tym, co zarobiłem na dorywczych pracach, ale miała udar w 2016 "
"roku i zostawiła mnie samego na ostatnie kilka lat, co spowodowało, że moje "
"oszczędności powoli wysychały, podczas gdy ja pracowałem przy byle jakich "
"śmieciowych robotach. Parę dni przed <the_cataclysm> dostałem zawiadomienie, "
"że bank będzie licytować moją gównianą małą przyczepę."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You have any kids?"
msgstr "Masz jakieś dzieci?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"Would you like to travel with me?  Someone good with a trade could be "
"helpful, and it's got to be better than wasting away here."
msgstr ""
"Czy chciałbyś ze mną podróżować? Ktoś dobry w handlu mógłby się przydać, a to "
"musi być lepsze niż marnowanie się tutaj."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I have a camp.  It's a damn sight better than those place, and there are "
"regular meals.  Someone with your trades experience would be welcome, even if "
"you can't do the big jobs anymore."
msgstr ""
"Mam obóz. Jest o niebo lepszy niż tamto miejsce, a posiłki są regularne. Ktoś "
"z twoim doświadczeniem w handlu byłby mile widziany, nawet jeśli nie możesz "
"już wykonywać ciężkich prac."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Yeah, we had two.  My daughter died of an OD right at the start of that "
"fentanyl stuff.  It did a real number on my son - they were twins you see - "
"and he cut ties to me and my wife.  Wasn't even there for her funeral.  I "
"can't blame him, it messed us all up pretty fierce.  As far as I'm concerned "
"he's still out there with my grandkids, hiding away somewhere safe.  These "
"days, no news is good news."
msgstr ""
"Tak, mieliśmy dwójkę. Moja córka zmarła z przedawkowania zaraz po pojawieniu "
"się tego całego fentanylu. To wywarło ogromny wpływ na mojego syna - byli "
"bliźniakami - i on zerwał więzi ze mną i moją żoną. Nie było go nawet na jej "
"pogrzebie. Nie mogę go winić, to nas wszystkich mocno sponiewierało. O ile mi "
"wiadomo, nadal jest z moimi wnukami, ukrywając się gdzieś w bezpiecznym "
"miejscu. W dzisiejszych czasach brak wieści to dobre wieści."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's sweet of you to say that, but I'm just not up to the wandering life, not "
"with these knees."
msgstr ""
"To miło z twojej strony, że tak mówisz, ale ja po prostu nie nadaję się do "
"wędrownego życia, nie z tymi kolanami."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"That's awful nice of you.  Tell you what: if you can help Dave get himself "
"sorted out, so I don't feel like I've gotta stay here keeping an eye on the "
"poor fella, then I'll come along."
msgstr ""
"To bardzo miło z twojej strony. Powiem ci coś: jeśli pomożesz Dave’owi "
"uporządkować swoje sprawy, tak żebym nie czuł, że muszę tu siedzieć i "
"pilnować biedaka, to pójdę z tobą."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I think I've sorted Dave out pretty well, don't you?  Would you consider "
"coming with me now?"
msgstr ""
"Myślę, że załatwiłem sprawę Dave’a całkiem nieźle, nie sądzisz? Czy rozważysz "
"teraz pójście ze mną?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid "Golly.  I didn't expect that, but I'm as good as my word.  <lets_go>"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Mutant beggar in the refugee center.
msgid "Yusuke Taylor"
msgstr "Yusuke Taylor"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
#. ~ Mutant beggar in the refugee center.
msgid "Computer Technician"
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "I couldn't help but notice, you're covered in fur."
msgstr "Nie sposób nie zauważyć, że pokrywa cię futro."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Would you like something to eat?"
msgstr "Czy chciałbyś czegoś do jedzenia?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I live here.  Too mutant to join the cool kids club, but not mutant enough to "
"kill on sight."
msgstr ""
"Mieszkam tu, Zbyt zmutowany by zasilić szeregi fajnych dzieciaków, ale nie na "
"tyle zmutowany by zabić bez zadawania pytań."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why live out here?"
msgstr "Czemu tu mieszkasz?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "You seem like you can hold your own.  Why not travel with me?"
msgstr "Wygląda na to, że potrafisz o siebie zadbać. Nie chciałbyś podróżować ze mną?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"It's safer than making my own home.  I head out and forage when I have to.  "
"As long as we keep it clean and do our part when a zombie comes, they let us "
"squat here as an extra defense.  They don't like that I've been bringing food "
"for the other squatters though… I think they are trying to slowly starve us "
"out, and even though I can't keep everyone's bellies full, I've been able to "
"bring back enough to keep these folk in better shape.  I suspect they'll find "
"an excuse to kick me out eventually."
msgstr ""
"To bezpieczniejsze niż zorganizowanie własnego miejsca. Wybywam na "
"poszukiwania jak potrzebuję. Póki dbamy o porządek i robimy swoje jak "
"nadchodzą zombie, pozwalają nam tu pomieszkiwać, jako dodatkowa ochrona. Nie "
"podoba im się natomiast, że przynoszę żywność dla pozostałych lokatorów… "
"Myślę, że chcieliby nas powoli zagłodzić i choć nie napełnię wszystkim "
"żołądków, to zdołam przynieść na tyle, by utrzymać tych gości w jako takiej "
"kondycji. Podejrzewam, że w końcu znajdą wymówkę, by mnie stąd w końcu "
"wywalić."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Gross, isn't it?  Feels like pubes.  I just started growing it everywhere a "
"little while after the Cataclysm.  No idea what caused it.  I can't blame "
"them for hating it, I hate it."
msgstr ""
"Ohyda, co nie? Są jak włosy łonowe. Zaczęły rosnąć gdzie popadnie zaraz po "
"Kataklizmie. Nie mam pojęcia co to spowodowało. Nie mam im za złe, że ich "
"nienawidzą, sam ich nienawidzę."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I do okay for myself actually.  I eat a lot of things close to spoilage while "
"I'm foraging.  If you've got food to spare, please give it to my friends."
msgstr ""
"Właściwie to dobrze sobie radzę. Podczas poszukiwań zjadam wiele rzeczy, "
"które są bliskie zepsucia. Jeśli masz coś do jedzenia, proszę, daj to moim "
"przyjaciołom."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Nothing too exciting.  I was in trade college, learning to be a computer "
"technician.  Those skills aren't too helpful, but when I was a kid I was an "
"Eagle scout.  I learned all kinds of useful stuff about plants and foraging, "
"and that's come in pretty handy."
msgstr ""
"Nic zbyt ekscytującego. Byłem w szkole handlowej, uczyłem się na technika "
"komputerowego. Te umiejętności nie są zbyt pomocne, ale kiedy byłem "
"dzieckiem, byłem Orlim Harcerzem. Nauczyłem się wielu przydatnych rzeczy o "
"roślinach i zbieractwie i to mi się bardzo przydało."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "What about your family, stuff like that?"
msgstr "A co z twoją rodziną i tak dalej?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"I don't want to think about it.  I grew up in Rhode Island, they're still "
"there.  I haven't heard from them since the insanity with the Governor and "
"that secession stuff.  All communication lines got closed off.  I haven't met "
"anyone who knows what happened to the people there but I don't have much hope."
msgstr ""
"Nie chcę o tym myśleć. Dorastałem w Rhode Island, oni nadal tam są. Nie "
"słyszałem o nich od czasu tego szaleństwa z gubernatorem i tą sprawą z "
"secesją. Wszystkie linie komunikacyjne zostały odcięte. Nie spotkałem nikogo, "
"kto by wiedział, co się stało z tamtejszymi ludźmi, ale nie mam zbyt wiele "
"nadziei."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Why don't you go back there?"
msgstr "Czemu tam nie wrócisz?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Could you tell me more about what happened with Rhode Island?"
msgstr "Możesz mi powiedzieć więcej na temat tego co wydarzyło się z Rhode Island?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Same reason as I'm stuck here… it's way too dangerous, for one thing.  Almost "
"a hundred miles, through zombie infested territory, on foot, to get to the "
"shoreline?  No, thank you.  And then, how would I get from the shore to Block "
"Island?  My family moved out there when Dad retired, and I get the impression "
"the ferry probably isn't running anymore.  Even if I got there, I don't know "
"what I'd find, and I think maybe that scares me the most."
msgstr ""

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"You don't know?  The governor went nuts, like a lot of people did leading up "
"to the end, only he had a lot more power to work with.  One day he just "
"showed up to work with a militia of rowdies and loyalists and staged a coup, "
"taking over the government completely, killing those that opposed him, and "
"moving as many people as he could get behind him onto the islands.  The "
"rumors I've heard is that most of them survived the Cataclysm and are still "
"running the show there, but that seems kind of impossible to me."
msgstr ""
"Nie wiesz? Gubernator oszalał, jak wielu ludzi przed końcem, tylko że miał o "
"wiele więcej władzy do dyspozycji. Pewnego dnia zjawił się w pracy z "
"bojówkami złożonymi z awanturników i lojalistów i dokonał zamachu stanu, "
"całkowicie przejmując władzę, zabijając tych, którzy mu się sprzeciwiali, i "
"przenosząc na wyspy tylu ludzi, ilu tylko zdołał zebrać. Słyszałem plotki, że "
"większość z nich przetrwała Kataklizm i nadal rządzi na wyspach, ale wydaje "
"mi się to niemożliwe."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Do you think you'd go back and look for your family?"
msgstr "Czy myślisz, że wróciłbyś tam i szukał swojej rodziny?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I've spoken to all your friends, and except for Dave, they're good to go.  "
"Dave wants to stay here.  How about you?"
msgstr ""
"Rozmawiałem z wszystkimi twoimi przyjaciółmi i z wyjątkiem Dave’a nie mają "
"nic przeciwko. Dave chce tu zostać. A ty?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ NPC dialogue line
msgid ""
"Huh.  Getting those three to sign on to a suicide mission is quite the feat… "
"sounds like you're pretty dedicated to this.  OK, I'm with you.  Let's round "
"up the others and hit the road."
msgstr ""
"Hę. Namówienie tej trójki na samobójczą misję to nie lada wyczyn… Wygląda na "
"to, że jesteś bardzo oddany tej sprawie. OK, jestem z tobą. Zbierzmy "
"pozostałych i ruszajmy w drogę."

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Right.  <lets_go>"
msgstr "Racja. <lets_go>"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
msgid "Aleesha Seward"
msgstr "Aleesha Seward"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Draco_Dune.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#. ~ Name suffix of a female NPC
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ Aleesha is fourteen and lost her family
#. ~ Name suffix of a male NPC
#. ~ Alonso wants to be the town bicycle, but isn't getting as much interest
#. as he'd hoped.  He'll trade a morale bonus for condoms.
#. ~ Boris is nice, but shy and sad.  He was a carpenter; he and his partner
#. lost their son in the Cataclysm, and it makes it harder for them to make
#. friends in the survivor group.
#. ~ Dana is a young woman who survived with her husband, but she was pregnant
#. and lost the baby.
#. ~ Draco is a middle-aged musician, and generally a pretty nice guy.  He's
#. always been a wanderer and this isn't his first time living basically
#. homeless.
#. ~ A welder, culturally muslim but only recently practicing since the
#. Cataclysm has made her rethink her connections to her family's religion
#. ~ Garry is a Stan's older brother.  He's grateful he's made it to help
#. support his brother, but he's very worried about Stan.
#. ~ Guneet is the Singhs' sixteen year old son.  Like his parents, he is
#. wracked with survivor's guilt for his family having made it out intact.
#. ~ Jenny Forcette is an experienced mechanical engineer.  Like the other
#. refugees in the center, she's terrified of the outside world.  Unlike many,
#. she has some ideas what to do about it.
#. ~ John is a pseudonym.  This guy probably lived in a city before the
#. Cataclysm, but now he either thinks he is or pretends to be a cowboy..
#. ~ Mandeep is the father of a small family.  They've made it through this
#. unscathed and have a lot of survivor's guilt as a result.
#. ~ Mangalpreet is the mother of a small family.  They've made it through
#. this unscathed and have a lot of survivor's guilt.
#. ~ Pablo is a young professional who survived with his wife, but she was
#. pregnant and lost the baby.
#. ~ A counselor from far away, Rhy can offer a lot of supports to player and
#. survivors if she can get herself sorted a little
#. ~ Stan is a broken man since he and Boris lost their son in the Cataclysm.
#. It might be possible to help put him back together slowly.
#. ~ A paramedic who suffers a bit of racism for being Asian
#. ~ Vanessa is a middle-aged hairdresser.  She doesn't want to talk about her
#. past.
msgid "Refugee"
msgstr "Uchodźca"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Alonso_Lautrec.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Dana_Nunez.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Fatima_Al_Jadir.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Garry_Villeneuve.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Guneet_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_John_Clemens.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mandeep_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Mangalpreet_Singh.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Pablo_Nunez.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Rhyzaea_Johnny.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Uyen_Tran.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Vanessa_Toby.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_teamster.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid ""
"I'm trying to put a cleanup crew together to tidy up the back room.  Can you "
"help?"
msgstr "Próbuję zebrać ekipę sprzątającą, żeby uporządkować zaplecze. Pomożesz?"

#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Aleesha_Seward.json
#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
msgid "Nice to meet you, kid.  What's up?"
msgstr "Miło mi cię poznać, dzieciaku. Co tam?"

